hadiths[543]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Book of Purification. Al-Lu'lu'i said: Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Sulayman ibn Abi al-Sa'ib informed us, from Talhah ibn Abi Qanan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to urinate, would go to rough, uneven ground, take a stick, poke the soil with it until it was loosened, then urinate."
"2","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from al-Hasan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered the privy, would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil and evildoing, filthy, impure, accursed Satan."
"3","Hisham ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Walid informed us, from Ibn Jabir, from Makhul, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade urinating at the doors of the mosque."
"4","Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, Waki' informed us, from Zam'ah ibn Salih, from Isa ibn Azdad, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you urinates, let him shake his private part three times."
"5","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah ibn Sufyan narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, from Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Qurashi, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you drink, sip your drink, and when you use the tooth-stick, use it across the teeth."
"6","What has come regarding ablution. Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Dimashqi Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us that Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to them; Sharik ibn Abi Namir narrated to me, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wash his face with his right hand."
"7","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad informed us, from Ishaq ibn Suwayd, from al-Ala ibn Ziyad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he performed the ritual bath, then saw a spot on his shoulder that the water had not reached, so he took a lock of hair from his head, squeezed it over his shoulder, then wiped his hand over that spot."
"8","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Za'idah informed us, Hisham narrated to us, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Abu al-Aliyah, who said: A man with impaired eyesight came and entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying with his Companions; he stumbled into a pit that was in the mosque, and a group of them laughed. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he ordered whoever had laughed among them to repeat the ablution and repeat the prayer. Abu Dawud said: This report was narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through al-Hasan, Ibrahim, and al-Zuhri, and all of their outlets go back to Abu al-Aliyah. Ibrahim narrated it from Abu Hashim al-Rummani, and al-Zuhri narrated it from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from al-Hasan. And Hafs al-Minqari said: I am the one who narrated it to al-Hasan from Abu al-Aliyah."
"9","Muhammad ibn al-Ala and Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, both saying: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, who said: A group from Banu Qushayr came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we travel in the land with our families, and we have no water with us except enough for our lips; may one of us be intimate with his wife? He said: Yes, even if it be for up to two years."
"10","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Layth informed us, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found blood on his garment and withdrew from prayer."
"11","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Jarir - meaning Ibn Hazim - narrated to us; I heard Abd al-Malik - meaning Ibn Umayr - narrating from Abdullah ibn Ma'qil ibn Muqarrin, who said: A Bedouin stood in a corner of the mosque, uncovered himself and urinated there. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the soil he urinated upon, throw it away, and pour water over its place. Abu Dawud said: It has been narrated with a connected chain, but it is not authentic."
"12","On prayer. Ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought them - meaning the prayers - to his people, he left them alone until, when the sun passed the middle of the sky, it was announced among them: Prayer in congregation. So they gathered for that, in alarm, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in four rak'ahs in which he did not recite aloud, with Jibril standing before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing before the people; the people followed their Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) followed Jibril, peace be upon him. Then he left them alone until, when the sun slanted while white and clear, it was announced among them: Prayer in congregation. They gathered for that, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in four rak'ahs, shorter than the Zuhr prayer; then Ibn al-Muthanna mentioned the same as he had mentioned about Zuhr. He said: Then he turned away from them until, when the sun had set, it was announced among them: Prayer in congregation. They gathered for that, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in three rak'ahs, reciting aloud in two rak'ahs and not reciting aloud in the third; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood before the people, and Jibril stood before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he mentioned the same as he had mentioned about Asr, until, when the twilight came and the night prayer was delayed, it was announced among them: Prayer in congregation. They gathered for that, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in four rak'ahs, reciting aloud in two and not reciting aloud in two - mentioning the same as he mentioned about Maghrib. He said: They spent the night not knowing whether anything would be added to that or not, until, when dawn broke, it was announced among them: Prayer in congregation. They gathered for that, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in two rak'ahs in which he recited aloud at length, with Jibril, peace be upon him, standing before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing before the people; the people followed their Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and their Prophet followed Jibril."
"13","Al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Juhani narrated to us; Waki' said: I think it is from al-Hasan ibn Salih, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasten the daytime prayer on a cloudy day, and delay the Maghrib."
"14","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Umarah, from Abu Mijlaz, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Umar to forbid urinating facing the qiblah of the mosque."
"15","Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Muradi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Ibn Lahi'ah, that Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj narrated to him that there were nine mosques in Madinah besides the mosque of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whose people would hear the adhan of Bilal in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pray in their mosques: the nearest of them, the mosque of Banu Amr ibn Mabdhul of Banu al-Najjar, the mosque of Banu Sa'idah, the mosque of Banu Ubayd, the mosque of Banu Salamah, the mosque of Banu Rabih of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, the mosque of Banu Zurayq, the mosque of Banu Ghifar, the mosque of Aslam, and the mosque of Juhaynah - with doubt about the ninth."
"16","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from al-Hadrami, from a man of the Ansar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you finds a louse while praying, let him not throw it away, but let him wrap it up until he finishes his prayer. Abu Dawud said: It was narrated from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, Anas ibn Malik and others that they used to kill lice and fleas during prayer."
"17","Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that the delegation of Thaqif came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a dome was pitched for them at the rear of the mosque so they could watch the prayer of the Muslims, their bowing and their prostration. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, would you lodge them in the mosque while they are polytheists? He said: The earth does not become impure; only the son of Adam becomes impure."
"18","Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Muradi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab; Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed me that Abu Sufyan used to enter the mosque in Madinah while he was a disbeliever - except that such is not permissible for him in the Sacred Mosque, because of what Allah said: The polytheists are impure, so let them not approach the Sacred Mosque - the verse."
"19","On the adhan. Abbad ibn Musa narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was concerned about the prayer, how to gather the people for it. So Abdullah ibn Zayd went away, concerned about the affair of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a visitor came to him in a dream and said to him: Tell the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to command a man, when the prayer time comes, to call the adhan, saying: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest - mentioning the adhan in pairs - and when he finishes, let him wait until the sleeper awakes and whoever wishes to perform ablution does so. When the people gather for their prayer, let him repeat, saying the same, until when he reaches: Come to prayer, come to success, let him say: The prayer has begun, the prayer has begun. Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah - and he narrated the hadith in full."
"20","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj; Ata informed me that he heard Ubayd ibn Umayr saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions consulted about how to appoint something by which they would gather for prayer when they wanted to; they considered the bell. While Umar ibn al-Khattab was about to buy two pieces of wood for a bell, Umar saw in a dream: Do not use the bell; rather, call the adhan for prayer. So Umar went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to tell him what he had seen, but revelation had already come with that; Umar was only surprised by Bilal calling the adhan. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Revelation has preceded you in that, when Umar told him of it."
"21","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us; Ata al-Khurasani narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Abdullah ibn Zayd and supplicated good for him, then left him, entered the mosque and said to his Companions: Advise us of something by which the people of the mosque may be summoned - and he narrated the hadith - and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Bilal, ascend, and he said to Abdullah ibn Zayd: Stand beside him and teach him the adhan."
"22","Harun ibn Sa'id al-Ayli narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us - (h) - and Makhlad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab; Hafs ibn Umar ibn Sa'd al-Mu'adhdhin informed me that Bilal came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the dawn prayer and was told: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is asleep. So Bilal said: Prayer - Makhlad said in his narration: in his loudest voice - prayer is better than sleep, and this was retained in the adhan of the Fajr prayer. And he said, from Hafs ibn Umar ibn Sa'd: My family narrated to me that Bilal..."
"23","Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in the year of the Conquest, ordered Bilal, who then called the adhan atop the Ka'bah."
"24","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu al-Mu'tamir - a shaykh of al-Hirah named Yazid ibn Tahman - from Ibn Sirin, that Bilal would place his fingers in his ears during part of his adhan or his iqamah, in a voice neither loud nor low. Abu Dawud said: His origin is Basran."
"25","Ahmad ibn Abi al-Hawari narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, from Abu Amr and others, from Ibn Harmalah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one leaves the mosque after the call except a hypocrite, except one whom some need takes out while he intends to return."
"26","On the congregation. Abu Tawbah narrated to us, al-Haytham - meaning Ibn Humayd - narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith and Zayd ibn Waqid, from Makhul and Yahya ibn al-Harith, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, both saying: A man entered the mosque having missed the prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will no man give charity to this one and complete the prayer for him? So a man stood and prayed with him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And this is part of the congregational prayer."
"27","Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, al-Khasib ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, regarding this report: Abu Bakr stood and prayed with him, though he had already prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Dawud said: This hadith, with this meaning, was also narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir, and Abu Ayyub al-Azdi."
"28","On garments. Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Isma'il - meaning Ibn Ayyash - narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Yahya ibn Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three whose prayer does not rise above their heads - and he mentioned the hadith - he said: And a woman who stands for prayer with her ear exposed."
"29","Hannad narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Abu al-Umayys, from Awn ibn Abdullah, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for prayer, nothing pleased him but clean garments and sweet fragrance."
"30","On the sutrah in prayer. Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us that he heard Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying toward a man, and ordered him to repeat the prayer. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have completed the prayer. He said: You prayed while looking at him, facing him."
"31","Umar ibn Hafs al-Wassabi narrated to us, Ibn Himyar - meaning Muhammad - narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Jabalah, from Khayr ibn Nu'aym, from Ibn al-Hajjaj al-Ta'i, in a marfu' report, who said: He forbade two men conversing while someone praying is between them. Abu Dawud said: He is Khayr ibn Nu'aym, who was a judge in Egypt."
"32","On the opening supplication. Abu Kamil narrated to us that Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to them; Imran ibn Muslim Abu Bakr narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he rose at night intending to pray tahajjud, would say before the takbir: There is no god but Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, Most Great. I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan, from his madness, his poetry, and his pride. He said: Then he would say: Allah is Greatest; and Imran raised his hands, demonstrating."
"33","Abu Tawbah narrated to us, al-Haytham narrated to us, from Thawr, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Tawus, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would place his right hand over his left hand, then press them both upon his chest while in prayer."
"34","On reciting Bismillah aloud. Abbad ibn Musa narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Sharik, from Salim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim aloud in Makkah. He said: The people of Makkah used to call Musaylimah al-Rahman, so they said: Muhammad is calling upon the god of Yamamah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded and concealed it, and he never recited it aloud until he died."
"35","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Husayn, from Abu Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to write: In Your name, O Allah. Then, when: Indeed, it is from Sulayman, and indeed, it is in the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate - was revealed, he wrote: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate."
"36","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not know the end of a surah until Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim was revealed. Abu Dawud said: This hadith has been given a connected chain, and this is more correct."
"37","On lightening the prayer. Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you leads the people in prayer, let him measure the prayer by the weakest among them, for behind him are the old, the weak, the needy, the sick, and the one far from home."
"38","Ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abbas al-Jushami, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the imams are drivers-away. Qatadah said: I know the drivers-away to be none but those who lengthen the prayer over the people until they drive them away from it."
"39","Ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Sawda, from Ibn Sabit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the dawn prayer and recited sixty verses, then heard the voice of a child, so he bowed; then he stood, recited two verses, then bowed."
"40","On recitation. Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Mu'adh ibn Abdullah ibn Khubayb, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr and recited in the first rak'ah: When the earth is shaken - then he stood for the second and repeated it."
"41","Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Muradi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yunus al-Ayli, from Ibn Shihab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established as sunnah that the recitation be aloud in both rak'ahs of the Fajr prayer; that in the first two rak'ahs of Zuhr one recites the Mother of the Qur'an and a surah in each rak'ah, silently to oneself; that in the last two rak'ahs of Zuhr one recites the Mother of the Qur'an in each rak'ah, silently to oneself; that the same be done in Asr as in Zuhr; that the imam recite aloud in the first two of Maghrib, reciting in each the Mother of the Qur'an and a surah; that in the last rak'ah of Maghrib one recites the Mother of the Qur'an; that in the last two rak'ahs one recites the Mother of the Qur'an silently to oneself; that those behind the imam remain silent and listen to what the imam recites aloud of the Qur'an, none reciting along with him; and that the tashahhud in prayer be when the imam and the people behind him sit in the first two rak'ahs."
"42","Yazid ibn Khalid narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Shaqiq Abu Layth; Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to me, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prostrated, his knees reached the ground before his hands. He said: And when he rose at the break between the two rak'ahs, he rose upon his knees, leaning on his thighs."
"43","Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Farwah, from Ibn Abi Layla, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed, if a jug of water were poured upon his back it would have settled upon it."
"44","Abu Tawbah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq - meaning al-Fazari - narrated to us, from Asim, from Ikrimah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying whose nose did not touch the ground, and said: Do not do that - or he said: A prayer in which the nose does not touch what the forehead touches is not valid. Abu Dawud said: This hadith has been given a connected chain, and this is more correct."
"45","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Ibn Sirin, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in prayer he would look this way and that; then, when: Successful indeed are the believers, those who humble themselves in their prayers - was revealed, he looked downward; and Abu Shihab said: with his sight toward the ground."
"46","Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib, from Abu Salih, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of whisperings in prayer, and he said: That is pure faith."
"47","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad - meaning Ibn Salamah - narrated to us, from Burd Abu al-Ala, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from a man of Banu Adi ibn Ka'b, that they entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying seated. They said: What is the matter with you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A scorpion stung me. Then he said: If one of you finds a scorpion while praying, let him kill it with his left sandal. Abu Dawud said: Sulayman did not meet this Adawi."
"48","Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, both saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Malik the nephew of Amr ibn Hurayth, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes touch his beard while praying."
"49","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, that Ibn Mas'ud came from Abyssinia and entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying. He greeted him, and he gestured to him with his head - or he said: he nodded with his head."
"50","On Friday. Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, who said: It has reached us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered the people of al-Awali in his mosque on Friday; those Muslims who were at al-Aqiq and the like would come to Friday. Abu Dawud said: Malik said: Al-Awali is three miles from Madinah."
"51","Abbad ibn Musa narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, who said: Women used to attend the Friday prayer with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"52","Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Amr narrated to us, from Wasil, from Mujahid, who said: The weak among the men and women would attend Friday with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then would not return to their lodgings until the next day, out of weakness."
"53","Al-Nufayli narrated to us; I read to Ma'qil ibn Ubaydullah, from al-Zuhri, that Mus'ab ibn Umayr, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to Madinah, led them in Friday prayer, and they were twelve men."
"54","On the Friday sermon. Abu Tawbah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Aban ibn Abdullah, who said: I was with Adi ibn Thabit on Friday, and when the imam came out - or he said: ascended the minbar - he turned to face him and said: This is what the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"55","Ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, and Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us; Ibn Wahb informed us, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, who said: It has reached us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would begin by sitting upon the minbar; when the mu'adhdhin fell silent, he stood and delivered the first sermon, then sat briefly, then stood and delivered the second sermon; when he finished it, he sought forgiveness, then descended and prayed. Ibn Shihab said: When he stood, he would take a staff and lean upon it while standing on the minbar; then Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, Umar ibn al-Khattab, and Uthman ibn Affan would do the same."
"56","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, who said: The opening of the sermon of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Praise be to Allah; we praise Him, seek His help, and seek His forgiveness. We seek refuge in Him from the evils of our souls. Whomever Allah guides, none can misguide, and whomever He sends astray, none can guide. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger; He sent him with the truth as a bearer of glad tidings and a warner before the Hour. Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger is rightly guided, and whoever disobeys them has gone astray. I ask Allah our Lord to make us among those who obey Him, obey His Messenger, follow His pleasure, and avoid His wrath; for we exist only through Him and for Him."
"57","Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Muradi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yunus, that he asked Ibn Shihab about the tashahhud of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Friday. Ibn Shihab said: Praise be to Allah; I praise Him and seek His help - then he mentioned the like of it exactly, meaning the like of the hadith of Uqayl."
"58","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, who said: It has reached us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when he preached he would say: All that is coming is near; what is coming is not far. Allah does not hasten for the haste of anyone, nor is He light for the sake of men's affairs. What Allah wills shall be, not what men will. Allah intends one thing and men intend another; what Allah wills comes to pass even if men dislike it. Nothing Allah has brought near can be distanced, and nothing He has distanced can be brought near. Nothing happens except by the permission of Allah, Majestic and Mighty."
"59","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Abu Imran al-Jawni informed us, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Ka'b al-Ahbar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite Hud on Friday. Abu Dawud said: Muslim said in this: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"60","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Ahmar, from Hisham, from his father, who said: The most frequent words of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he sat upon the minbar were: Fear Allah and speak a right word."
"61","Qutaybah narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Ibn Shihab, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat upon the minbar on Friday to supplicate, he would only point with his finger while the people said amen."
"62","Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us; Abu Mu'adh Bukayr ibn Ma'ruf informed me that he heard Muqatil ibn Hayyan saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Friday before the sermon, like the two Eids, until one Friday, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was preaching - having already prayed Friday - a man entered and said: Dihyah ibn Khalifah has arrived with his merchandise; and when Dihyah arrived, his family would meet him with tambourines. So the people went out, thinking there was nothing wrong in leaving the sermon. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, then revealed: And when they see merchandise or amusement, they disperse toward it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put the Friday sermon first and delayed the prayer. No one would leave for a nosebleed or ritual impurity after the prohibition except by seeking the permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), gesturing to him with the finger next to the thumb, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would grant him permission by gesturing with his hand. Some hypocrites found the sermon and sitting in the mosque burdensome; when a Muslim man sought permission, the hypocrite beside him would rise, concealing himself with him, until he left. Then Allah, Majestic and Mighty, revealed: Allah surely knows those of you who slip away, concealing themselves - the verse."
"63","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would speak between his descent from the minbar and his entry into prayer. Abu Dawud said: This has also been narrated with a connected chain, but it is not strong and is not authentic."
"64","Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Zayd, who said: Jarir ibn Hazim and I were with Thabit al-Bunani, when Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, do not stand until you see me. So Jarir thought that Thabit had narrated it from Anas. In the Dar al-Sumay'i edition there is an unnumbered report after this hadith: Abu Dawud said: I heard Ahmad ibn Hanbal mention the hadith of Jarir ibn Hazim, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, do not stand until you see me. Ahmad said: They claim Hammad ibn Zayd said: Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman narrated it to Thabit from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father; but Jarir thought Thabit narrated it from Anas, so he narrated it thus."
"65","On the two Eids. Ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Sa'id - meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub - from Abu Isa al-Khurasani, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade bringing weapons out on Eid day."
"66","Abu Tawbah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Makhul, who said: The spear was carried with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only because he used to pray toward it."
"67","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah ibn Sufyan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Zuhri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say the takbir from the beginning of the days of Tashriq until the end of the days of Tashriq. Abu Dawud said: It has reached me from Ahmad that he said: Shu'bah visited Ibn Abi Dhi'b and forbade him from narrating this hadith, meaning the hadith of Ibn Abi Dhi'b from al-Zuhri about the takbir."
"68","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Tawbah al-Anbari, from al-Sha'bi, who said: Al-Baqi' was swept for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a day of Fitr or Adha."
"69","On seeking rain. Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Malik, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, give drink to Your servants and Your beasts, spread Your mercy, and give life to Your dead land."
"70","Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Sharik ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Namir, from Ata ibn Yasar, that a man from Najd came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in drought and shall perish unless Allah reaches us with mercy; so supplicate to Allah to send us relief. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated, and the man returned having received rain, and they lived through that year. Then a man returned the following year and said: O Messenger of Allah, you supplicated to Allah for us and He gave us life the first year, so supplicate to Allah for us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Like the rain of the disbelievers? No; go back."
"71","On travel prayer. Al-Nufayli narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Sa'id ibn al-As, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Madinah, he would shorten the prayer at al-Aqiq; and when he left Makkah, he would shorten at Dhu Tuwa. Abu Dawud said: It has been narrated with a connected chain, but it is not authentic."
"72","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash informed us, from Ibrahim, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I am a merchant who travels to Bahrain; so he ordered him to pray two rak'ahs."
"73","On voluntary prayer. Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Makhul, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays two rak'ahs after Maghrib before speaking, they are written - or raised - for him in Illiyyun."
"74","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Faris narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, the nephew of Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle; Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq informed me that it reached him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Our Lord descends in the last part of the night, and a caller calls out in the highest heaven: Has not the Creator descended? So the inhabitants of heaven prostrate, and a caller calls out among them to that effect, passing no inhabitants of a heaven but that they are in prostration. Abu Dawud said: Sufyan - meaning al-Thawri - used to dislike imagining the modality of this hadith and the like."
"75","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Nasr narrated to us. He said: I asked Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, saying: O Abu Muhammad, I wish to ask you something. He said: Do not ask. I said: If I do not ask you, whom shall I ask? He said: Ask. I said: What do you say about these narrated hadiths, such as: The hearts are between two fingers, and that Allah laughs, or marvels, at one who remembers Him in the markets? He said: Let them pass as they came, without asking how."
"76","On prostration. Muhammad ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, who said: A boy recited the verse of prostration before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the boy waited for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to prostrate, and when he did not prostrate, he said: O Messenger of Allah, is there not a prostration in it? He said: You are the one who recited it; had you prostrated, we would have prostrated."
"77","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Mahri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us; Hisham ibn Sa'd and Hafs ibn Maysarah informed me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, who said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)... and he mentioned the like of it."
"78","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Amir ibn Jushayb, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Surah al-Hajj has been favored over the rest of the Qur'an with two prostrations. Abu Dawud said: This has also been given a connected chain, but it is not authentic."
"79","On Laylat al-Qadr. Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Khaldah narrated to us; I heard Abu al-Aliyah narrating that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying and said to him: When is Laylat al-Qadr? He said: Seek it in the first night and the last night, and in the odd nights."
"80","On supplication. Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Ali ibn Abi Talib, who had gone out for the Fajr prayer, while Ali was saying: O Allah, forgive me; O Allah, have mercy on me; O Allah, accept my repentance. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck his shoulder and said to him: Generalize - for the merit of the general over the particular is like that between heaven and earth."
"81","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah and Humayd ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, from Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, from Abdullah ibn Bujayr, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never heard one praising Allah, Mighty and Majestic, without prolonging the praise with him. Humayd said in his narration: Bishr narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Bujayr ibn Humran al-Qaysi narrated to us."
"82","On one who sleeps through prayer. Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ali ibn Amr, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept through the morning prayer and awoke, he said: We shall surely enrage Satan as he enraged us. So on that day he recited Surah al-Ma'idah in the Fajr prayer."
"83","Comprehensive matters of prayer. Al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Hassan informed us, from Muqatil ibn Hayyan, in a marfu' report, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man comes and finds no one, let him draw a man from the row to himself to stand with him; how great is the reward of the one drawn out!"
"84","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Mahri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Ibn Lahi'ah and Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bakr ibn Sawadah al-Judhami, from Salih ibn Khaywan al-Saba'i, who narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying, prostrating upon his forehead while wrapped over his brow, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) uncovered his forehead."
"85","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us; al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah narrated to me that Wahib ibn Abdillah al-Ma'afiri narrated to him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you place his garment upon his nose in prayer, for that is the muzzle of Satan."
"86","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, from Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam, from Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb, that a cat wanted to pass before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, so he held it back with his foot."
"87","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Haywah ibn Shurayh informed us, from Salim ibn Ghaylan, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by two women praying and said: When you prostrate, press some flesh to the ground, for the woman is not like the man in that."
"88","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman and others informed me, from Ibn al-Had, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ammar, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when Dhu al-Yadayn spoke to him, stood, said the takbir, prayed two rak'ahs with the people, gave the salutation, and prostrated twice."
"89","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Mu'awiyah ibn Salih informed me, from Abd al-Qahir, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was supplicating against Mudar, Jibril came to him and gestured to him to be silent, so he fell silent. He said: O Muhammad, Allah did not send you as one who reviles or curses; He sent you only as a mercy, and did not send you as a punishment: It is not for you to decide anything, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers. He said: Then he taught him this qunut: O Allah, we seek Your help and Your forgiveness; we believe in You and humble ourselves to You; we cast off and abandon whoever disbelieves in You. O Allah, You alone we worship, to You we pray and prostrate, to You we hasten and hurry; we hope for Your mercy and fear Your severe punishment; indeed Your punishment overtakes the disbelievers."
"90","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us; Ibn Jurayj narrated to me that Ibn Shihab informed him that the people, when the mu'adhdhin said Allahu Akbar to establish the prayer, would rise for prayer, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not come to his place of prayer until the rows were straightened."
"91","Ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih informed me, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah sealed Surah al-Baqarah with two verses which He gave me from His treasure beneath the Throne, so learn them and teach them to your women and children, for they are prayer and Qur'an and supplication."
"92","Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, Ibn Idris informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Umarah informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Hazm, he said: In the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - meaning this one - was: None touches the Qur'an except one who is pure."
"93","Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm, that the letter which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to 'Amr ibn Hazm stated: None touches the Qur'an except one who is pure."
"94","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shu'ayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: I read a document with the family of Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm, mentioning that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote it to 'Amr ibn Hazm when he appointed him over Najran, and he narrated the hadith in it, including: The lesser Hajj is 'Umrah, and none touches the Qur'an except one who is pure. Abu Dawud said: This hadith has been narrated with a connected chain, but it is not authentic."
"95","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Separate Sha'ban from Ramadan."
"96","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Khalid - meaning Ibn Durayk - from Ibn Muhayriz, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deem the pre-dawn meal desirable even if only sips of water."
"97","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are two dawns. As for the one that is like the tail of the wolf, it permits nothing and prohibits nothing. As for the spreading one that covers the horizon, it permits prayer and prohibits food."
"98","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Isma'il, from Hakim - meaning Ibn Jabir - he said: I was told that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was eating the pre-dawn meal when Bilal came to him and said: Prayer, O Messenger of Allah. He remained silent and gave him no reply. So Bilal returned and said: Prayer, O Messenger of Allah, morning has come upon you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on Bilal; were it not for Bilal I would have hoped that concession would be granted to us until sunrise."
"99","Musaddad narrated to us, from Hushaym, from Husayn, from Mu'adh ibn Zuhrah, that it reached him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he broke his fast, would say: O Allah, for You I fasted, and upon Your provision I broke my fast."
"100","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id informed us, and Ibn Wahb - both said: Al-Layth narrated to us, from 'Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no showing off in fasting."
"101","'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Talq ibn Habib, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I had intercourse with my wife in Ramadan ... and he narrated the hadith. He said: Then a basket containing fifteen sa' of dates, amounting to sixty quarters, was brought. He said: Feed sixty poor persons with this. He said: There is no one between its two lava plains more in need of it than us. He said: Then go and feed it to yourself and your family."
"102","Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, from 'Ata' ibn 'Abdullah al-Khurasani, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that he said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) striking his neck and tearing his hair, saying: The far one is ruined. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is that? He said: I had intercourse with my wife in Ramadan while fasting. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Can you free a slave? He said: No. He said: Can you offer a camel as sacrifice? He said: No. He said: Then sit down. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a basket containing dates. He said: Take this and give it in charity. He said: O Messenger of Allah, no one is more in need than I. He said: Eat it, and fast one day in place of what you did. Malik said: 'Ata' said: I asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib how many dates were in that basket. He said: Between fifteen sa' and twenty sa'."
"103","Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from al-Qasim ibn 'Asim, he said: I said to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib: A hadith that 'Ata' al-Khurasani narrated to us from you - what is it? I said: Concerning the one who had intercourse with his wife in Ramadan. He said: Freeing a slave or a sacrificial offering. He said: 'Ata' lied; rather it was so-and-so - pointing to his house - who had intercourse with his wife in Ramadan and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Do you have anything? He said: No. He said: Sit down. He said: Then a basket containing twenty sa' or thereabouts was brought. He said: Give this in charity. Isma'il said: I think Khalid said: I have no food for my family. He said: Then feed it to your family."
"104","Ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Rufay', from Tawus, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he set out on a journey at the beginning of the day, would break his fast, and when he set out after the sun had declined, he would not break his fast."
"105","Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Anbari narrated to us, Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn Sulaym al-Bahili, from al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guard your wealth with zakah, treat your sick with charity, and meet the waves of calamity with supplication and humility."
"106","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Hammad said: I said to Qays ibn Sa'd: Take for me the letter of Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm. So he gave me a letter, reporting that he had taken it from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote it to his grandfather. I read it, and in it was mention of what is due from the obligations on camels. He narrated the hadith until reaching one hundred and twenty; if they are more than that, then count a hiqqah for every fifty, and any remainder returns to the first obligation of camels. Whatever is less than twenty-five, sheep are due for it: for every five camels one sheep, among which there is no male, no old animal, and no defective sheep."
"107","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, and Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, that Mu'adh ibn Jabal was brought, from Yemen, the young cattle and sheep below the zakah threshold, and he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me nothing concerning either."
"108","'Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Malik, from Humayd ibn Qays, from Tawus al-Yamani, that Mu'adh ibn Jabal took from thirty cows a tabi' and from forty cows a musinnah. He was brought less than that and refused to take from it, saying: I heard nothing from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning that until I meet him and ask him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died before Mu'adh ibn Jabal arrived."
"109","Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, Ibn Thawr narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar said: Simak ibn al-Fadl gave me a letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Malik ibn Kaflanis and al-Muqawqis, in which was: For cattle the same as for camels."
"110","With the same chain from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said, from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah: For every five cows and for ten, two sheep; for fifteen, three sheep; and for twenty, four sheep. Al-Zuhri said: When they are twenty-five, one cow is due up to seventy-five, in which two cows are due up to one hundred and twenty; if they exceed one hundred and twenty, then for every forty cows one cow. Ma'mar said: Al-Zuhri said: It has reached us that their saying - the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For every thirty cows a tabi', and for every forty cows a cow - was a concession for the people of Yemen, then this came after that."
"111","Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, Ibn Thawr narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, he said: For a time I used to hear them saying: Take from us what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took, and I wondered why that was not accepted from them, until al-Zuhri told me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote these obligations but died before writing to his officials. Abu Bakr acted upon what he wrote, mentioning cattle as well as far as I know."
"112","Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri mentioned that among what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) firmly established concerning charity was that he set, for the awqas of cattle after his first letter with Mu'adh ibn Jabal - the awqas being five cows up to ten - for ten, two sheep; then he made the charity on cattle similar to the charity on camels."
"113","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from 'Urwah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man to collect charity and ordered him to take the young she-camel, the old she-camel, and the defective one, but beware of the choicest of their property."
"114","Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Abu Salamah al-Khurasani narrated to us - al-Hasan said: he is Ghalib ibn Sulayman - Kathir Abu Sahl narrated to us, while we were in Khurasan, from al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has overlooked for you three things: the forehead, the nukhkhah, and the kusa'. Kathir said: They held that the forehead means horses, the nukhkhah means working and water-drawing camels, and the kusa' means small sheep."
"115","Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Ghalib ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Ziyad, from al-Hasan, with the same hadith, and he said: The nukhkhah means small sheep, and the kusa' means donkeys."
"116","Kathir ibn 'Ubayd al-Madhhiji narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Rashid, from Makhul, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not buy back charities until they are restrained and branded. Abu Dawud said: This is also narrated as the saying of Makhul."
"117","Muhammad ibn Qudamah ibn A'yan narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to Mu'adh ibn Jabal while he was in Yemen: Upon every adult male and female is a dinar or its equivalent in Ma'afiri garments, and no Jew shall be turned away from his Judaism."
"118","'Abdullah ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Wahb, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from Makhul, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be lenient with people in estimation of fruits, for among wealth are the 'ariyyah; another narrator said: and the watiyyah. Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, 'Umar narrated to us: I asked al-Awza'i, he said: The watiyyah is whoever treads among the people. Abu Dawud said: The correct word is al-watiyyah, meaning one who frequents the land and eats from it."
"119","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn al-Harith, from Yazid ibn 'Abdullah ibn Qusayt, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed zakat al-fitr as two mudds of wheat."
"120","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid - meaning Ibn Musafir - from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed zakat al-fitr as two mudds of wheat."
"121","Qutaybah narrated to us, al-Layth informed us, from 'Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, likewise from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"122","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, he said: If I did not hear it from al-Zuhri, then Sufyan ibn Husayn informed me of it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the same meaning."
"123","'Abdullah ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded zakat al-fitr with the same meaning."
"124","Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, 'Abd al-Khaliq al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: Charity in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and 'Umar was half a sa' of wheat. Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah and Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated it likewise from 'Abd al-Khaliq."
"125","Nasr ibn 'Asim al-Antaki narrated to us, that Anas ibn 'Iyad informed them from al-Harith - meaning Ibn 'Abd al-Rahman - he said: I asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib: Is zakat al-fitr due on shepherds and farm workers? He said: Yes; it is but zakat al-fitr; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that it be paid on behalf of the young and the old, the free and the slave, the shepherds and the farm workers."
"126","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, a man at Mina who was beside Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me; I asked Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr about him and he said: This is so-and-so son of 'Abdullah ibn Zayd - the caller of the adhan. I asked that man and he told me from his father that 'Abdullah ibn Zayd gave a walled garden of his in charity. His parents came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, nothing sustained us but it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned it to his parents, then they died and he inherited it from them afterwards."
"127","'Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Ja'far, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade harvesting by night and cutting dates by night."
"128","Ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from 'Ali ibn al-Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade harvesting by night, cutting dates by night, and reaping by night; that was because a caretaker of his cut dates by night."
"129","'Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Naysaburi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim al-Juddi informed us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ja'far, with its chain, likewise. Ja'far said: We think he disliked that only because the poor and needy do not witness it."
"130","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah ibn Sufyan narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from 'Udhafir al-Basri, from al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever pays the zakah of his wealth has fulfilled the duty upon him, and whoever adds is better."
"131","Muhammad ibn 'Awf al-Ta'i narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Musa ibn Sulayman narrated to me, I heard al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever earns wealth through sin, then joins kinship with it, gives it in charity, or spends it in the path of Allah, all of it will be gathered together and cast with him into Hell."
"132","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, Abu Nawfal - meaning Ibn Abi 'Aqrab - narrated to us, he said: 'A'ishah said: O Messenger of Allah, where is 'Abdullah ibn Jud'an? He said: In the Fire. She said: It weighed heavily upon her. He said: O 'A'ishah, what weighed heavily upon you? She said: He used to feed food and join kinship. He said: It will be lightened for him because of what you mention."
"133","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: When the verse 'Pilgrimage to the House is a duty to Allah upon people who can find a way to it' was revealed, it was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the way? He said: Provision and a mount."
"134","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, he said: I heard an old man narrating to Abu Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I wish to renew in the hearts of the believers: any child whose family performs Hajj with him and then he dies, it suffices for him; if he grows up, Hajj is obligatory upon him. And any slave whose family performs Hajj with him and then he dies, it suffices for him; if he is freed, Hajj is obligatory upon him."
"135","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Fudayl narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed al-Tan'im as the miqat for the people of Makkah. Abu Dawud said: Sufyan said: This hadith is not known. Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Razi narrated to us, Mihran narrated to us, he said: Sufyan said: This is hardly known, meaning the hadith of al-Tan'im."
"136","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Harmalah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One in ihram may kill the wolf ... and he mentioned the hadith."
"137","Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Ziyad informed me, from Abu al-Zinad, he said: It reached me from 'A'ishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled concerning ostrich eggs: for each egg, fasting one day or feeding a poor person. Abu Dawud said: This hadith was given a connected chain, and this is the correct one."
"138","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated to us, Matar al-Warraq narrated to us, that Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah told them from a man of the Ansar that a man in ihram trampled an ostrich nest with his mount. The man went to 'Ali and asked him about that. 'Ali said to him: For each egg, the striking of a she-camel or a camel fetus. The man went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him what 'Ali had said. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Ali has said what you heard, but come to the concession: upon you for each egg is fasting one day."
"139","Abu Tawbah narrated to us, Mu'awiyah - meaning Ibn Sallam - narrated to us, from Yahya, Yazid ibn Nu'aym or Zayd ibn Nu'aym - Abu Tawbah doubted - informed me, that a man from Judham had intercourse with his wife while both were in ihram. The man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said to them both: Complete your rites and offer a sacrifice, then return until, when you are at the place where you did what you did, separate so that neither of you sees the other. Upon you both is another Hajj; come forth until, when you are at the place where you did what you did, enter ihram, complete your rites, and offer a sacrifice."
"140","Ishaq ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated on the night of the Ifadah on his mount, touching the Corner with his staff and kissing the staff."
"141","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, 'Ata' informed me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastened in all his 'Umrahs at the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and Abu Bakr hastened in the year of Hajj when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him, then Abu Bakr, 'Umar, 'Uthman, and the caliphs successively hastened likewise. Abu Dawud said: This hadith has been given a connected chain, but it is not authentic, and this is the correct one."
"142","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Rawh and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, 'Ata' informed me, he said: It is thought that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) camped on the night of Muzdalifah at the present stations of the imams. Ibn Bakr said: I think."
"143","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Zabban ibn Salman narrated to me, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) camped on the day of 'Arafah by the rock facing the stations of the rulers at 'Arafah in the low land of the mountain, screening its people with a garment over him."
"144","Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came to Makkah, prayed with one adhan and one iqamah, prayed at Mina with one iqamah, prayed at 'Arafah with two iqamahs, at Muzdalifah with two iqamahs, and prayed at al-Abtah in the valley on the day of departure the Zuhr, 'Asr, Maghrib, and 'Isha'."
"145","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, that Yahya, Rawh, and Ibn Bakr told them the meaning, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: 'Ata' said: It reached me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the adhan in the evening - meaning the evening of 'Arafah - and the iqamah on the night of Muzdalifah. Abu Dawud said: Yahya said: An iqamah, an iqamah. Abu Dawud said: This was given a connected chain, but it is not authentic."
"146","Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Hannad narrated to us, both said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one of the two prayers at 'Arafah with an adhan and an iqamah."
"147","Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, 'Umar - meaning Ibn 'Abd al-Wahid - narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Sulayman ibn Musa, he said: It is not preserved from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he raised his hands with full raising except in three places: asking for rain, asking for victory, and the evening of 'Arafah; thereafter there was a lesser raising."
"148","Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, 'Awwam informed us, from al-Saffah ibn Matar, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Asid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The day of 'Arafah is the day on which people stand at 'Arafah."
"149","Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn 'Allaq narrated to us, from Yazid ibn 'Ubaydah, he said: In the year in which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, the people performed Hajj without an imam."
"150","Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Muhammad ibn Qays ibn Makhramah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed on the day of 'Arafah and said: This is the day of the Greater Hajj. Those before you among the people of idols and ignorance would depart when the sun was seen upon the mountains as though it were the turbans of men, and would push forth from Muzdalifah when it shone upon the mountains as though they were the turbans of men. Our guidance differs from the guidance of the people of polytheism and idols."
"151","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Tawus said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) camped to the left of the imam's prayer place at Mina. Others of our shaykhs besides Tawus said like the saying of Tawus, adding: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded his wives to camp beside the house - his house at Mina - commanded the Ansar to camp in the ravine behind the house, and said to the people: Camp, pointing to the areas of Mina."
"152","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, 'Ata' informed me, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to permit the sacrificial camel, when its owner needed it, to be loaded and ridden without exhaustion. I said: What? He said: For the walking man, the one following on the way, and if it gives birth, its calf and its equivalent are carried upon it."
"153","'Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, that Sulayman ibn Hayyan told them from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata' al-Khurasani, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: A sacrificial camel is due upon me, I can afford it but cannot find one. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Slaughter seven sheep."
"154","Al-Walid ibn 'Utbah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Damrah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, with its chain and meaning."
"155","Muhammad ibn al-Musaffa al-Himsi narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to me, from Yahya, from 'Ikrimah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed his garments at al-Tan'im."
"156","Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd al-Muharibi - a Kufan - narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash, Sa'id ibn Yusuf narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from 'Ikrimah the freedman of Ibn 'Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed his garments at al-Tan'im while in ihram."
"157","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, from Waki', from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Salih ibn Abi Hassan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man in ihram girded with a shiny rope and said: O owner of the rope, cast it off."
"158","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah ibn Sufyan narrated to us, al-Walid informed us, from 'Ali - meaning Ibn Hawshab - I heard Makhul say: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a garment saturated with safflower dye and said: O Messenger of Allah, I wish to perform Hajj; may I enter ihram in this? He said: Do you have another? She said: No. He said: Then enter ihram in it."
"159","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Bakr - meaning Ibn Mudar - narrated to us, from 'Umarah ibn Ghazziyyah, from Ibn Shihab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stoned the farthest Jamrah, returned to the slaughter place, sacrificed, shaved, then hastened to the Tawaf immediately."
"160","Ibn Khallad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform the Tawaf every night of the nights of Mina. Abu Dawud said: This has been given a connected chain."
"161","'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, and Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, that Jarir told them, from Mansur, from Ibrahim: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept on the night of departure at al-Abtah a sleep, then set out before dawn. Qutaybah did not mention the night of departure."
"162","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Mahri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub informed me, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Ibn Shihab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Hakim ibn Hizam to trade in cloth and food, and forbade him from trading in slaves."
"163","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Sinan, from 'Abdullah al-Muktib - and he is 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith - he said: A camel was led past the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being with the people. One of the people said: For how much did you take it? He said: For such-and-such. He added to the price. When he returned home he said: I lied to people among whom was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him of the addition. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give the excess in charity."
"164","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deceit, trickery, and treachery are in the Fire."
"165","Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Alqamah, from Ibn Abi Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The owner of the goods is most entitled to seek a price."
"166","Abu Tawbah narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed a Bedouin selling something and said: Keep to the first offer and the first market, or the first offer; for profits lie with leniency."
"167","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Abu Ya'qub al-Thaqafi, from Khalid - meaning Ibn Abi Malik - he said: I sold goods to Muhammad ibn Sa'd and he said: Give me your hand so I may clasp it, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Blessing lies in hand-clasping."
"168","Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Anbari narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Mujahid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a foal from a Bedouin for one hundred sa' of dates. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man among them: Go and tell them to measure until they receive in full - meaning the measure. The man went out rubbing with his elbows, meaning he hurried."
"169","Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thawr narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: There were debts upon men in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); we know of no free man sold for a debt."
"170","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Mahri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid informed me, from Ibn Shihab, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b ibn Malik informed me, that Mu'adh ibn Jabal - one of his people, the Banu Salamah - fell heavily into debt in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did no more for his creditors than strip him of his wealth for them."
"171","Muhammad ibn al-Mutawakkil al-'Asqalani and Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Sufyan narrated to us, both said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik - Ibn Dawud named him 'Abd al-Rahman - that Mu'adh ibn Jabal kept borrowing until all his wealth was consumed. His creditors came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Mu'adh asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to ask his creditors to remit or delay, but they refused. Had they spared anyone for anyone's sake, they would have spared Mu'adh for the sake of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sold all his wealth for his debt until Mu'adh was left with nothing."
"172","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged with the meaning of al-Zuhri's hadith, adding: If anything remained from its price, it is shared with the creditors. Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that whoever dies with another man's goods intact in his possession, without having paid anything from its price, the owner of the goods shares with the creditors in it."
"173","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la ibn 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Burd, from Sulayman ibn Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed a man selling food adulterated with barley and said: Separate this from this and this from this, then sell each as you wish; for there is no cheating in our religion."
"174","Isma'il ibn Mas'adah al-Tunukhi narrated to us, Abu Tawbah narrated to us, Mus'ab ibn Mahan al-'Asqalani narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Rashid, from Makhul, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed a man selling wheat, mixing the good with the bad, forbade him and said: Distinguish each one separately."
"175","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade adulterating milk for sale. Abu Dawud said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim likewise narrated it from Yunus; and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from Yunus, from al-Hasan, who said: 'Umar said."
"176","'Abd al-Salam ibn 'Atiq al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Mushir narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to me, Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi narrated to me from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling a living animal for a dead one."
"177","Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling meat for a live animal."
"178","Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Hamadhani and Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Mahri narrated to us, both said: Ibn Wahb informed us, Musa ibn Shaybah al-Hadrami informed me from Yunus ibn Yazid, from 'Umarah ibn Ghazziyyah al-Ansari, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he and Abu Bakr left Makkah migrating to Madinah, passed a shepherd of sheep; they bought from him a sheep, stipulating that its wool remain his."
"179","Ahmad ibn Sa'id and Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, al-Layth informed me, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from 'Umarah ibn Ghazziyyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the same hadith."
"180","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hiring a worker without clarifying - meaning until clarifying - his wage for him."
"181","Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Do not sell the wool of sheep while it is on their backs, and do not sell their milk while it is in their udders."
"182","Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Umar ibn Farrukh, from Ikrimah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the same meaning."
"183","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Umar ibn Farrukh narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Zubayr, from Ikrimah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper his wage, a dinar."
"184","al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ikrimah ibn Ammar; Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: (Then contract them in writing, if you know any good in them). He said: If you know they have a trade, and do not send them out as a burden upon people."
"185","On pledges: Muhammad ibn Ubayd [ibn Hisab] narrated to us, [Muhammad ibn Thawr narrated to us,] from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The pledge shall not be forfeited. I said to him: What do you think of your statement, ""The pledge shall not be forfeited"" - is it a man saying: If I do not bring you your money, this pledge is yours? He said: Yes. [He said:] And it later reached me that he said: If it perishes, the right of this one is not lost; it perished at the loss of the owner of the pledge; its benefit is his and its liability is upon him."
"186","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed: The pledge shall not be forfeited; its benefit belongs to its owner and its liability is upon him."
"187","Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak informed us, from Mus'ab ibn Thabit. I heard Ata narrating that a man pledged a horse and it died in his possession, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the pledgee: Your right is gone."
"188","Abdullah ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Mihran, from Zam'ah, i.e. Ibn Salih, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The pledge stands for what it secures."
"189","Ali ibn Sahl al-Ramli narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Amr narrated to us, from Ata, that a man pledged a horse and the horse died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The pledge stands for what it secures."
"190","Hannad [ibn al-Sari] narrated to us, from Ibn Abi al-Zinad, from his father, that people misunderstand the statement of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), ""The pledge stands for what it secures""; he only said that concerning what the trustworthy one among the jurists informed us of: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The pledge stands for what it secures when it perishes and its value is unknown. It is then said to the one who pledged it: You claimed its value was one hundred dinars, yet you took twenty dinars for it and accepted the pledge; and it is said to the other: You claimed its price was ten dinars, yet you accepted it as recompense for twenty dinars."
"191","On a man finding his property with another: Harun ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid. Usayd ibn Hudayr ibn Simak narrated to me - Harun said: Ahmad, meaning Ibn Hanbal, said to me: In his book, [meaning Ibn Jurayj's,] it is Usayd ibn Zuhayr, but thus he narrated to them at Basra - that Mu'awiyah wrote to Marwan: If a man finds his stolen property in the hand of a man, he is most entitled to it. So Marwan wrote to me of that while I was over al-Yamamah, and I wrote to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed that if he finds it in the hand of a man who is not suspect, he may either take it for what it was bought for, or pursue his thief; and Abu Bakr and Umar decreed likewise after him. So Marwan sent my letter to Mu'awiyah, and Mu'awiyah wrote to Marwan: Neither you nor Usayd shall decree against me in what I have been put in charge of; rather I shall decree against you both, so carry out what I have decreed. So Marwan sent Mu'awiyah's letter to me, and Usayd said: The [Prophet] (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar decreed thus; by Allah, I shall never decree otherwise."
"192","Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, from Musa ibn al-Sa'ib, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever finds his very property with a man is most entitled to it, and the buyer pursues the one who sold to him."
"193","On gifts: al-Abbas ibn al-Walid ibn Mazyad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from al-Awza'i, who said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is revoked from the charity of one who acts unjustly in his life what is revoked from the bequest of one who acts unjustly at his death. al-Abbas said: He narrated it to us once from Urwah, and once from Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Dawud said: This hadith is not sound; its raising to the Prophet is not sound."
"194","Sulayman ibn Dawud [al-Mahri] narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us; Yunus ibn Yazid and Ibn Sam'an informed me, from Ibn Shihab, who said: There is revoked from the injustice of a living giver in his life what is revoked from the injustice of a dead person in his bequest at his death."
"195","Muhammad ibn Yahya [ibn Faris] narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to me, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, who said: There is revoked from the injustice of a living giver what is revoked from the injustice of a dead person in his bequest. Abu Dawud said: al-Hiql narrated it from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, as a stopped report."
"196","On emancipation: Muhammad ibn Rafi and Yahya ibn Musa al-Balkhi narrated to us, both said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Umar ibn Hawshab informed us, Isma'il narrated to me - and Yahya said: Isma'il ibn Umayyah - then both agreed: from his father, from his grandfather, who said: They had a slave called Tahman - or Dhakwan - and his grandfather freed half of him, so the slave came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You become free in your freedom and remain a slave in your slavery. So he would serve his master until he died; Yahya added: meaning he was a slave one month and free one month. Abu Dawud said: His grandfather is Amr ibn Sa'id ibn al-As."
"197","On tawliyah: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bazzaz narrated to us, Mansur ibn Salamah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, who said: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib said, in a report which he raised as though to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There is no harm in tawliyah (resale at cost) of food before taking possession of it, no harm in iqalah (cancellation) of food before taking possession of it, and no harm in partnership in food before taking possession of it."
"198","On marriage: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, Husayn al-Mu'allim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast, and spare your hair, for it causes foulness."
"199","Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Tawus, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no zimam in Islam and no celibacy in Islam."
"200","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Husayn, from Abu Malik, concerning His statement: (O you who believe, do not forbid the good things Allah has made lawful for you). He said: It was revealed concerning Uthman ibn Maz'un and his companions; they had forbidden themselves many pleasures and women, and one of them intended to cut off his male organ; so Allah revealed this verse: (And do not transgress; indeed Allah does not love the transgressors)."
"201","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us; and Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Maymun Abu Mughallis, from Abu Najih - Ahmad [ibn Hanbal] said: he is the father of Abdullah ibn Abi Najih - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever can afford to marry yet does not marry is not of me."
"202","al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Marry women, for they will bring you wealth."
"203","Abu Tawbah al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Abu Damrah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, concerning His statement: (And made you kings). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - or, I only know that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A wife, a dwelling, and a servant."
"204","Kathir ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from al-Zubayr ibn Sa'id al-Hashimi, from his shaykhs, raised to the Prophet: Keep to mothers of children, for they are blessed in womb."
"205","Kathir ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Abu Saba' Utbah ibn Tamim, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ka'b ibn Malik, that he wanted to marry a Jewess, so [the Messenger of Allah] (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do not marry her, for she will not keep you chaste."
"206","al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn bint Dawud [ibn Abi Hind], among the best of men, narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Isma'il al-Makki, from Ziyad al-Sahmi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade seeking a foolish woman as a wet nurse, for milk transmits likeness."
"207","Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Salamah al-Makhzumi, from Isa ibn Talhah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a woman for her kinship, out of fear of severing ties."
"208","Musa narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have an orphan girl in my care; shall I marry her? He said: What do you think - if she were ugly and had no wealth, would you marry her? He said: No. He said: Then choose the best on her behalf."
"209","Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from Yunus, [from al-Hasan, who] said: A man said to Ali something like it."
"210","On dower: [Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Suwayd ibn Manjuf] narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah; he heard Abdullah ibn Kulayb al-Sadusi [narrating], from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make the private parts of women lawful to you with the best of your wealth."
"211","Isa ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Damrah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Bakr, from Makhul, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever makes the private part lawful, whether a gift or present, counts as part of the dower."
"212","Harun ibn Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad - meaning Ibn Rashid - narrated to us, from Makhul, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever makes the forbidden lawful, whether a gift or a promise, belongs to her; and the most deserving of what a man honors is his daughter [and his sister]. Abu Dawud said: [Something similar has been narrated with a connected chain]."
"213","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Ja'far, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Thawban, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever uncovers a woman and looks at her private parts, the dower becomes due."
"214","Hannad narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Umayr al-Khath'ami, from Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah al-Ta'ifi, from Ibn al-Baylamani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: (And give women their dowries as a gift). They said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the ties between them? He said: Whatever their families mutually agree upon."
"215","On looking when proposing marriage: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to propose to a woman, so he sent a woman to her and said: Smell her sides of the mouth and look at her ankles."
"216","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Shabib ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Muqatil ibn Hayyan, that [the Prophet] (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he married off his daughters, would order that their husbands not approach them until they had bathed, and would order their husbands to do so."
"217","al-Hasan ibn Amr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Ziyad, meaning Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill, he sought his wives' permission to be nursed in the house of Aishah, and they permitted him."
"218","Ahmad ibn Abi al-Hawari narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on one of his campaigns, saw a slave girl large of breast and belly, and said: What is this? They said: So-and-so bought her from the captives. He said: Does he have intercourse with her? They said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How can he bequeath to it when he has betrayed it in its hearing and sight, or how can it bequeath to him when it is not of him? I have intended to curse him with a curse that will enter the grave with him. [He said:] And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed her child. Abu Dawud said: Its beginning is narrated with a connected chain, and this adds: And he freed her child."
"219","Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Sumay' narrated to us. I heard Abu Razin al-Asadi saying: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to him: What do you think of the statement of Allah the Exalted: (Divorce is twice; then keeping with kindness or releasing with kindness)? He said: Then where is the third? He said: Releasing with kindness, [the third]."
"220","Ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a bedouin to marry a Muhajir woman. And al-Hasan used to say: If he stays with her in the town, there is no harm."
"221","Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Hakam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to a youth from the kings of Yemen for his sister, and he married her to him, so he went to fetch her. When he came to his father, he said: You have married a woman of royal daughters to a commoner; he kept at him until he consented. So he brought her, and when he went in to her, she said: I seek refuge with Allah from you. So he said: You have indeed sought refuge with a Refuge, and he let her go."
"222","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, from Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal, that Umm Habibah was succeeded in marriage by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Uthman ibn Affan married her to him in the land of Abyssinia, and her mother was the daughter of Abu al-As, the paternal aunt of Uthman ibn Affan."
"223","On marrying equals: Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Ibn Hurmuz al-Fadaki narrated to us, from Sa'id and Muhammad, the two sons of Ubayd, from Abu Hatim al-Muzani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one comes to you whose religion and character you approve of, marry him to her - three times."
"224","Qutaybah [ibn Sa'id] narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Abdullah ibn Hurmuz al-Yamani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the same; he said: The people pressed him, so he repeated it three times. Abu Dawud said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman has transmitted it with a connected chain from Ibn Ajlan, and it is a mistake."
"225","Abdullah ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Bilal to a household of the Ansar to propose to them, and they said: A black Abyssinian slave! So Bilal said: Had the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not commanded me to come to you, I would not have come to you. They said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded you? He said: Yes. They said: You have taken possession. So he came [to] the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him, and a piece of gold was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gave it to him and said: Drive this to your wife; and he said to his Companions: Gather for your brother for his wedding feast."
"226","Uthman narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Amir, who said: Bilal went with his brother to propose on his behalf to some people of the Arabs, and they said: Two Abyssinian slaves! [So Bilal said: Yes,] we were astray and Allah guided us, and we were slaves and Allah - [the Mighty and Majestic] - freed us."
"227","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah; he mentioned it, from Muharib, who said: If you marry us, praise be to Allah; and if you turn us away, Allah is Greatest."
"228","Harun ibn Zayd narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Zayd ibn Aslam, that Banu Bukayr came to [the Messenger of Allah] (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Marry our sister to so-and-so. He said: Why not Bilal? They repeated, and he repeated the words three times, so they married her to him. He said: Banu Bukayr were among the Emigrants of Banu Layth."
"229","Amr ibn Uthman and Kathir ibn Ubayd narrated to us, both said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, al-Zubaydi narrated to me; al-Zuhri narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Banu Bayadah to marry Abu Hind to a woman of theirs, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we marry our daughters to our freedmen? So Allah - [the Mighty and Majestic] - revealed: (Indeed We created you from male and female and made you peoples and tribes) - the verse. al-Zuhri said: It was revealed specifically concerning Abu Hind. Abu Dawud said: Part of it has been narrated with a connected chain, and it is weak."
"230","Isa ibn Yunus al-Tarsusi narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Amr ibn Dinar: that Bilal had under him a Qurayshi woman."
"231","Ibn Ubayd narrated to us, in the hadith of Hammad from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, that a man married his daughter while she was unwilling, so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: Do you dislike him? She said: Yes, so he put her affair in her own hand."
"232","On divorce: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Awf, from Anas ibn Sirin, who said: It reached me that Abu Ayyub - meaning he intended to divorce Umm Ayyub - consulted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Divorcing Umm Ayyub is a grave sin."
"233","Ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, that Ghaylan ibn Salamah embraced Islam while having ten wives, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to keep four of them."
"234","Muhammad ibn Khallad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj; Ata informed me, who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining of her husband, and he said: Will you return his garden to him? She said: Yes, and more. He said: As for the more, no."
"235","Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us. He said: And Dawud ibn Abi Asim said: He informed that Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed him that a woman who was under Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas - and he had given her a garden as dower, and he was jealous, so he struck her and broke her hand - came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained of him to him, and said: I shall return his garden to him. So he called her husband and said: She returns your garden to you. He said: And is that mine? He said: Yes. He said: I have accepted, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go, and it is one. Then she married al-Rifa'ah al-Amiri after him, and he struck her, so she came to Uthman and said: I shall return his dower to him. So Uthman called him and he accepted, and Uthman said: Go, and it is one."
"236","Ishaq ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning a woman who seeks khul': He shall not take from her more than he gave her."
"237","Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade taking from a woman who seeks khul' more than he gave her. Abu Dawud said: Waki said: I asked Ibn Jurayj about it, [and he denied it and did not recognize it]."
"238","On declaring unlawful: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared his Coptic slave girl Mariyah, the mother of Ibrahim, unlawful, so he was commanded to expiate for his oath, and he was reproached for that."
"239","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the house of Hafsah, and she came in and saw his slave girl with him, and said: In my house [and on my day]? He said: Be quiet; by Allah, I shall never approach her, and she is unlawful for me."
"240","On hudud: Hisham ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Khushani narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Makhul, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Establish the hudud, in settlement and travel, upon the near and the far, and do not care in Allah's cause for the blame of any blamer."
"241","al-Abbas al-Anbari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri: that Safwan ibn al-Mu'attal struck Hassan ibn Thabit with the sword in the time of [the Messenger of Allah] (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not cut off his hand."
"242","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Isa - meaning Ibn Abi Azzah - from al-Sha'bi, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he cut off (the hand) for the value of five dirhams."
"243","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a thief who had stolen a shawl, and he said: We do not think you stole? He said: Indeed, I did. So he said: Take him away, cut him off, then cauterize him, then bring him to me. So they took him, cut him off, then cauterized him, then brought him to him, and he said: Repent to Allah. He said: I have repented to Allah. He said: O Allah, accept his repentance."
"244","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not cut off for food."
"245","[Abu Ma'mar] narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from al-Husayn [ibn Dhakwan], from Yahya, from Ba'jah ibn Abdullah al-Juhani, that a man of Juhaynah stole goods from the market and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have stolen, [so cut off my hand.] So he cut off his hand, then he raided in the path of Allah and was martyred."
"246","Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Anbari narrated to us, [Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us,] from Ibn Jurayj, from Abd Rabbih ibn Abi Umayyah, from al-Harith ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Rabi'ah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a thief, and it was said: He belongs to orphans of the Ansar who have no wealth besides him, so he let him off; then a second time, and he let him off; then a third time, and he let him off; then a fourth time, and he let him off; then a fifth time, and he cut off his hand; then a sixth time, and he cut off his foot; then a seventh time, and he cut off his hand; then an eighth time, and he cut off his foot; then he said: Four for four."
"247","Kathir ibn Ubayd narrated to us, [Baqiyyah narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us;] al-Fudayl ibn Fadalh al-Hawzani narrated to me, who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, there is an event in my belly - and he mentioned [the story of stoning] - so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Stone her, increase the stones around her, and keep pelting her."
"248","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from al-Hasan al-Basri, who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have committed adultery - and he mentioned the hadith. He said: When she gave birth, he ordered her, so she purified herself and put on her shrouds, then he ordered concerning her and she was stoned."
"249","On blood-money, concerning a Muslim being executed for a disbeliever he killed: [Ibn Abi Najiyah] al-Iskandarani narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Sulayman [ibn Bilal] narrated to me, Rabi'ah narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani; he narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a Muslim man who had killed a covenanted person of the dhimmah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought the Muslim forward and his neck was struck, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the worthiest to fulfill his covenant. Ibn Wahb said: Its explanation is that he killed him treacherously."
"250","[Wahb ibn Bayan, Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Hamadhani, and Ibn al-Sarh said:] Ibn Wahb informed us, Abdullah ibn Ya'qub informed me; Abdullah ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Salih al-Hadrami narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed, on the day of Khaybar, a Muslim for a disbeliever he had killed treacherously, and said: I am the worthiest - or most entitled - to fulfill his covenant."
"251","When retaliation is taken for wounds: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Muhammad ibn Talhah, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and a man had struck him with a horn - and said: O Prophet of Allah, grant me retaliation. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Wait until you heal. Then he came to him and said: O Prophet of Allah, grant me retaliation. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Wait until you heal. Then he came to him a third time and said: O Prophet of Allah, grant me retaliation, so he granted retaliation. Then the one retaliated against healed, while the leg of the one granted retaliation remained lame, so he said: O Prophet of Allah, my leg is lame, so grant retaliation. He said: Go, retaliation has been granted for you."
"252","[Ibn Abdah] and Ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, both said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah ... with the same meaning. Ibn al-Sarh said in it: I already told you."
"253","Musaddad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, with his chain, likewise. Abu Dawud said: Ibn Ulayyah transmitted it with a connected chain, from Ayyub, from Amr, from Jabir, and erred in it; the first is more sound."
"254","How much is the blood-money: al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Juhani narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Makhul, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while the blood-money was eight hundred dinars, then Umar after him feared, so he made it twelve thousand dirhams or one thousand dinars."
"255","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb: that the value of the blood-money in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was eight hundred dinars."
"256","Wahb ibn Bayan, Ibn al-Sarh, and Ahmad ibn Sa'id said: Ibn Wahb informed us, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, who said: I read in the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Amr ibn Hazm when he sent him to Najran - and the letter was with Abu Bakr ibn Hazm - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote in it: This is an exposition from Allah and His Messenger: (O you who believe, fulfill contracts). And he wrote verses from it until he reached: (Indeed Allah is swift in reckoning). Then he wrote: This is the book of wounds: For a life, one hundred camels; for the nose when its severing is complete, one hundred camels; for the eye, fifty camels; for the ear, fifty camels; for the hand, fifty camels; for the foot, fifty camels; for every finger of those, ten camels; for the ma'mumah (wound reaching the brain membrane), a third of a life; for the ja'ifah (piercing wound), a third of a life; for the munaqqilah (bone-displacing fracture), fifteen; for the mudihah (bone-exposing wound), five camels; and for a tooth, five camels. Ibn Shihab said: This is what I read in the letter the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote, which was with Abu Bakr ibn Hazm. Abu Dawud said: This has been transmitted with a connected chain but is not sound; Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated it from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from his father, from his grandfather."
"257","Abu Hubayrah narrated to us, who said: I read it in the original of Yahya ibn Hamzah; Sulayman ibn Arqam narrated to me. And Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us; my father and my uncle narrated to me, both saying: Yahya ibn Hamzah, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, likewise. Abu Dawud said: What Sulayman ibn Dawud said, he erred in."
"258","al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Dawud [al-Khawlani - trustworthy -], from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from his father, from his grandfather; al-Hakam erred in it."
"259","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Amr ibn Hazm, who said: In the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - meaning this one - was: For the male organ, the blood-money; and for the tongue, the blood-money."
"260","Musa narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Makhul, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the tongue, the blood-money; for the male organ, the blood-money; and for the front teeth, five obligations each."
"261","Muhammad ibn [Abdullah] narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Maghra, narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us. I heard Makhul saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed the blood-money for the two testicles."
"262","Qutaybah narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn al-Had, from Ibn Shihab, who said: [The Messenger of Allah] (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the spine, the blood-money."
"263","On the blood-money of a dhimmi: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya Abu Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood-money of every covenanted person, while in his covenant, is one thousand dinars."
"264","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Faris narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, who said: [The Messenger of Allah] (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the male organ, the blood-money."
"265","[And with the same chain:] That [the Prophet] (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed for the two hands the blood-money, and for the two feet the blood-money."
"266","[And with the same chain:] From al-Zuhri, that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The woman - her paternal relatives pay her blood-money, and her sons inherit from her. Abu Dawud said: Yahya ibn Yaman narrated it from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from al-Mughirah, and it is a mistake."
"267","Muhammad ibn al-Wazir al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Yahya, meaning Ibn Hassan, narrated to us, Mujammi' ibn Ya'qub narrated to us. Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman informed me, who said: The blood-money of a dhimmi was like that of a Muslim in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the time of Abu Bakr, the time of Umar, and the time of Uthman, until it was the beginning - meaning of the rule of Mu'awiyah - when Mu'awiyah said: If his family have been afflicted by his loss, the treasury of the Muslims has been afflicted by his loss as well; so make for the treasury of the Muslims half, and for his family half: five hundred dinars and five hundred dinars. Then another man of the dhimmah was killed, and Mu'awiyah said: If we were to look at what enters the treasury and make it a stipend for the Muslims and their defense - he said: from then on he fixed his blood-money at five hundred."
"268","On qasamah: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah and Asim al-Ahwal, [both] from Abu al-Mughirah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) exacted retaliation on the basis of qasamah at Ta'if."
"269","Mahmud ibn Khalid and Kathir ibn Ubayd narrated to us, both said; (transformation) and Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah ibn Sufyan narrated to us; al-Walid informed us, from al-Awza'i, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb - Ibn al-Sabbah said in his narration: that he narrated to him from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - that he killed, on the basis of qasamah, a man of Banu Nasr ibn Malik at Bahrar al-Rugha'; Mahmud added: on the bank of Liyyah; the killer and the killed were of them. [Abu Dawud said:] And Mahmud is the firmest of them in this hadith; and Kathir said: at Buhayr al-Rugha'."
"270","Harun ibn Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us. Makhul narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not decree retaliation in qasamah."
"271","Muhammad ibn Sama'ah al-Ramli narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, he said: I said to Ubaydullah ibn Umar: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put to death on the basis of qasamah (collective oaths)? He said: No. I said: Then Abu Bakr? He said: No. I said: Then Umar? He said: No. I said: Then how do you put to death on its basis? He fell silent. (He said:) Then I met Malik ibn Anas and said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put to death on the basis of qasamah? He said: No. I said: Then Abu Bakr? He said: No. I said: Then Umar? He said: No. I said: Then why do you put to death on its basis? He said: We do not relegate the statement of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to deception."
"272","Muhammad ibn Qudamah ibn A'yan narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman; Abu Raja', the freedman of Abu Qilabah, narrated to me, from Abu Qilabah, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said: What do you say concerning qasamah? The people clamored, then he said: What do you say, O Abu Qilabah, and he set me up before the people; so he mentioned the hadith of the Uraniyyun. I said: There was in this matter a precedent (sunnah) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): a group of the Ansar were talking with him one night, then one of them went out ahead of them, then they went out after him and found their companion weltering in blood. They returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we left you and our companion went out ahead of us, and we went out after him and found him weltering in blood. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and said: Whom do you suspect - or whom do you think - killed your companion? They said: We think the Jews killed him. He summoned the Jews and said: Did you kill this man? They said: No. He said: Will you accept the oaths of fifty Jews that they did not kill him? They said: They would not care if they killed us all and then swore. He said: Then will you establish the blood-money, with fifty of you swearing that they killed him? They said: We would never swear. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid his blood-money himself."
"273","Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath, from al-Hasan: A man slapped his wife's face, so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained to him, saying: Retaliation. Then there was revealed: (Men are caretakers of women), so he abandoned it (retaliation)."
"274","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Imran ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib narrated to us, my father Muhammad ibn Sa'id informed me, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held liable every two combatants who meet in fighting for whatever occurs between them, when they confess or when clear proof is established. Abu Dawud said: Al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wada'ah and Yunus ibn Yusuf narrated this report from Ibn al-Musayyib, from Uthman ibn Affan, as his own statement, and did not raise it (to the Prophet)."
"275","Regarding jihad: Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, he said: It has reached us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never allotted to an absent person from spoils he had not witnessed except on the day of Khaybar, when he allotted to the absent ones of the people of al-Hudaybiyah, because Allah had granted Khaybar to the Muslims among the people of al-Hudaybiyah, and He said: (Allah has promised you abundant spoils that you will take, and He hastened this one for you). So it belonged to the people of al-Hudaybiyah, those of them who witnessed it and those who were absent from it, and to whoever witnessed it along with them from others. And it has reached us that he allotted to Uthman on the day of Badr, and it has reached us that he allotted to Talhah and Sa'id ibn Zayd, though they were absent in Sham."
"276","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Mas'udi, from al-Hakam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted shares to Ja'far and his companions, though they arrived after Khaybar; he allotted to them from it although they had not witnessed the fighting."
"277","Abu Salih narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj; Abu Uthman ibn Yazid informed me, he said: This continued to be acted upon, and they raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If a child is born to a man after he has left the land of the Muslims and the land of truce, while he is in the land of the enemy - even if that was the very first place he entered - that newborn has a share along with the Muslims. He said: And they named the man concerning whom the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed for his child (thus): if a man dies after entering the land of the enemy and leaving the land of the Muslims and the land of truce, his share belongs to his family."
"278","Abu Salih narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Simt, from al-Nu'man, from Makhul, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted at Khaybar to (some) women a share each."
"279","Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, and Amr informed me, that Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal informed him, that Ibn Shibl narrated to him that Sahlah bint Asim was born on the day of Khaybar, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She has come with ease, then he struck a share for her. A man from the people said: You have given Sahlah the like of my share!"
"280","Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from al-Zuhri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought the help of some Jews in his war and allotted shares to them."
"281","Al-Qa'nabi and Hannad narrated to us - al-Qa'nabi said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us - from Haywah ibn Shurayh, from Ibn Shihab, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted shares to Jews who had raided along with him - Hannad added: the like of the shares of the Muslims."
"282","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn al-Hurr; al-Hakam narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to grant additional grants (nafal) before the obligation of the fifth (khums) was revealed; when there was revealed: (Know that whatever you take as spoils, a fifth of it is for Allah), he abandoned the grants he used to give, and that became part of the fifth of the fifth, which is the share of Allah and the share of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"283","Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Zayd, from al-Hakam, from a man, from his father, concerning the spoils of war (anfal), he said: (They ask you about the spoils), and in the reading of Ibn Mas'ud it is: (They ask you (for) the spoils). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to grant whatever he wished from the spoils, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted to Sa'd ibn Malik the weapons of al-Asi ibn Sa'id on the day of Badr, and Sa'd had killed al-Asi. Then that was abrogated by: Know that whatever you take as spoils, a fifth of it is for Allah; and in the reading of Abdullah it is: (Whatever you take as spoils belongs to Allah and the Messenger). The spoils would be taken and a fifth of them set aside, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would grant from the fifth of the fifth his own share. And the ruler today may grant from the share of Allah and the Messenger whatever he wishes, for it is only the fifth of the fifth - he has nothing besides it."
"284","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq; Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr informed us, he said: The raid of Qurayzah was the first raid in which shares were cast and the portions marked out; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the horseman three shares and the footman one share, and the horses were thirty-six."
"285","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Shu'aythi narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted two shares to the Arabian (horse) and one share to the crossbred (hajin)."
"286","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, Hammad ibn Khalid and Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to them the same meaning, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Abu Bishr, from Makhul, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared the crossbred as crossbred on the day of Khaybar and the Arabian as Arabian: for the Arabian two shares and for the crossbred one share."
"287","A chapter on horses and riding animals: Hannad narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Rashid, he said: It was said to Makhul: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim did not allot shares to horses from the fortress of Tustar - a fortress he had conquered. So Makhul said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted shares to horses on the day of Khaybar, though it was only a fortress."
"288","Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, al-Nu'man informed me, from Makhul, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted on the day of Khaybar two shares to the horses, one share to the footman, one share to the children, and one share to the women."
"289","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from a man of the people of Makkah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided an expedition and they gained booty, so he allotted to the horseman three shares, to the footman one share, and to the mailed (armored) fighter two shares."
"290","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, from al-Zubayr, meaning Ibn al-Khirrit, from Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a horse, so he went to it and wiped its face, its eyes and its nostrils with the sleeve of his shirt. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, do you wipe with the sleeve of your shirt? He said: Gabriel has reproached me concerning horses."
"291","Al-Walid ibn Utbah narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, Ali ibn Hawshab narrated to us; he heard Makhul saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wipe (and rub) the horses and cover them with cloths."
"292","Abdullah ibn al-Jarrah and Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Waki' narrated to us, from Masarrah ibn Ma'bad, from al-Wadin - Muhammad ibn Sulayman said: al-Wadin ibn Ata' - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not lead horses by their forelocks so as to humiliate them."
"293","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Wa'il - or Bakr ibn Wa'il - from al-Zuhri, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Delay the loads, for hands are suspended and feet are shackled."
"294","A chapter on misappropriation of spoils (ghulul): Ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, from al-A'mash, from Shimr, from Abu Hazim, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a leather mat from the spoils, and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, this is for you, to shade yourself from the sun with. He said: Would you like your Prophet to be shaded by a mat of the Fire?"
"295","Concerning the carrying of heads: Abdullah ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Usamah, from Bashir ibn Uqbah, from Abu Nadrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met the enemy and said: Whoever brings a head shall have from Allah whatever he wishes. Two men came with a head and disputed over it, so he awarded it to one of them and said: Wish from Allah whatever you will. He said: I wish a sharp sword with which I fight until I am killed. Abu Dawud said: There are hadiths on this subject from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), none of which is sound."
"296","On crucifixion: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, Abu al-Haytham narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) crucified Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt to a tree. He said: O Messenger of Allah, am I (singled out) apart from Quraysh? He said: Yes. He said: Then who will care for the children? He said: The Fire."
"297","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from al-Hasan, he said: The idolaters offered ounces of gold to a man to kill the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seized him and crucified him on a mountain in Madinah called Dhubab; he was the first one crucified in Islam."
"298","On riding animals: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Abu al-Anbas, from Zadham, he said: Ali saw three (men) on a mule and said: Let one of you descend, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the third."
"299","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Ansari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever rides a mount without reins or a halter and it throws him off ... then he spoke stern words concerning it."
"300","Muhammad ibn Rafi' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Atash, narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Amr narrated to us, from al-Wadin - and in my view he is Ibn Ata' - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever walks beside a camel for a turn (uqbah) shall have (a reward) equal to (freeing) a slave."
"301","Abu Salih narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj; Muhammad ibn Murrah informed me that the name of the sword of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was Dhu al-Faqar, and the name of the armor of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was Dhat al-Fudul."
"302","A chapter on the excellence of jihad: Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, from Ibn Jabir, from Makhul, that he used to narrate to them from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: A pilgrimage for one who has not performed pilgrimage is better for him than ten raids, or nine raids; and a raid after pilgrimage is better than ten pilgrimages, or nine."
"303","Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, from Makhul, he said: Those seeking permission to (go for) pilgrimage pestered the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Tabuk expedition, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A raid for one who has already performed pilgrimage is better than forty pilgrimages."
"304","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abdullah al-Awdi narrated to us, that Wabarah Abu Kurz al-Harithi narrated to them that he heard Rabi' ibn Ziyad saying: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was traveling, he came upon a boy of Quraysh walking apart from the road. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is that not so-and-so? They said: Yes, indeed. He said: Then call him. He said: Why have you kept away from the road? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I disliked the dust. He said: Do not keep away from it, for by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, it is indeed the fine dust of Paradise."
"305","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah: Some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came praising a companion of theirs, saying: We have never seen the like of so-and-so at all; whenever we were marching he was engaged in recitation, and whenever we halted he was engaged in prayer. He said: Then who used to take care of his work? ... until he mentioned: And who used to feed his camel or his animal? They said: We did. He said: Then all of you are better than him."
"306","Mahdi ibn Hafs narrated to us, Isa narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ma'mar, from Musa ibn Shaybah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lives in the desert for more than two months, it is a bedouin life."
"307","Musa narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at al-Batha when Yazid ibn Rukanah - or Rukanah - came upon him with some goats of his and said to him: O Muhammad, will you wrestle me? He said: What will you wager? He said: A sheep from my flock. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrestled him and threw him, and took a sheep. Then Rukanah stood up and said: Will you do it again? He said: What will you wager? He said: Another. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrestled him and threw him. He said to him the like of that, then he said: What will you wager? He said: Another. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrestled him and threw him - he mentioned that several times - then he said: O Muhammad, by Allah, no one has ever laid my side on the ground, and it is not you who has thrown me - meaning: so he accepted Islam - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for him."
"308","Abu Tawbah al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will remain in my community a righteous company; they will not call upon Allah for anything but He will answer them. Through them you are aided, through them you are given rain, and I think he said: And through them harm is repelled from you."
"309","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Safwan, meaning al-Marwani, narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b; Salih ibn Kathir - and he was a companion of Ibn Shihab - informed me, he said: Ibn Shihab set out for a journey on Friday morning, so I spoke to him about that, and he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out for a journey on Friday morning."
"310","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata', he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to travel alone or to spend the night alone in a house."
"311","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ikrimah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man called al-Fajr to the people of Makkah concerning some matter of his. Abu Dawud said: Something similar in meaning is narrated with a connected chain."
"312","Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Haywah, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of companions are four, the best of detachments are four hundred, and the best of armies are four thousand."
"313","Makhlad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Uthman, meaning Ibn Umar, narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ... with the same meaning. Abu Dawud said: This has been narrated with a connected chain, but it is not sound; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated it with a chain, and that is an error."
"314","Abu Salih Mahbub ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Ishaq informed us, from Yazid ibn al-Simt, from al-Nu'man, from Makhul, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised Abu Hurayrah, then said: When you go on a raid and meet the enemy, do not be cowardly; when you gain (spoils), do not misappropriate; do not harm a believer; do not disobey one in authority; do not burn palm trees, and do not drown them. He said: So Abu Hurayrah used to inform the people of them."
"315","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Mahri narrated to us - Ibn Wahb informed us - Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim, the freedman of Abd al-Rahman: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised a man who went on a raid, saying: Do not cut a fruit-bearing tree, do not kill a beast for which you have no need, and beware of harming the believers."
"316","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marched to al-Ta'if and ordered the fortress of Malik ibn Awf demolished, and ordered the grapevines cut."
"317","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought counsel on the day of Badr, so al-Hubab ibn al-Mundhir said: We think all the wells should be filled in except one well, so that we meet the people - meaning the enemy - at it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered all those wells filled in except the well of Badr, and they met the people at it. And he consulted the people when he came to Khaybar as to where to camp, so al-Hubab said: Camp - meaning between the fortresses - so that we cut off news of these from those, and news of those from these. So he camped among the palaces."
"318","Abu Tawbah narrated to us, Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Abu Sallam saying: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came down at Khaybar, he fought in one quarter of it, then moved to another quarter. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are moving to the side of the town, so let no one fight where we used to fight. They set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as his detachments, but a man from the chiefs of the Ansar, along with a group of his companions, acted contrary and fought where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had forbidden them. He was killed, and they brought him carried. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to pray over him, then turned and said: Was he killed before we forbade, or after we forbade? They said: After you forbade. So he turned away from him, then ordered the caller to call out among the people: Paradise is not lawful for a disobedient one. Then he was left lying until the end of the day, when a group of his people came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Shall we not bury him? He said: Do whatever you wish."
"319","Harun ibn Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa' narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, he said: A man charged the enemy and said: I am the Persian boy. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Why did you not say: I am the Ansari boy? And he was a freedman of the Ansar."
"320","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Ata' al-Khurasani, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, all of Banu Salamah fight; among them are those who fight for worldly gain, those who fight out of courage, and those who fight seeking the Face of Allah - so which of them is the martyr? He said: All of them, so long as the basis of his affair is that the word of Allah be supreme."
"321","Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan: A man wanted to charge the idolaters alone, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you think you will kill them alone? Wait until your companions charge, then charge along with them."
"322","Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us; I heard Abu Uthman saying: I heard al-Hasan saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is overwhelmed by his sins, let him place the passes of the Romans behind his back. Abu Dawud said: I think Abu Uthman is Jisr ibn al-Hasan al-Basri."
"323","Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guards the frontier behind the settled land of the Muslims for forty days, Allah will grant him, in place of everyone he left behind him - of protected people, dhimmis, and the livestock in their hands - a qirat, a qirat, of reward."
"324","Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that the Arabs be fought for (acceptance of) Islam, and nothing besides it be accepted from them; and he commanded that the People of the Book be fought for (acceptance of) Islam, and if they refused, then the jizyah."
"325","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: The companions of Musaylamah seized two men of the Muslims and brought them to Musaylamah. He said to one of them: Do you bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. He said: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: I am deaf - three times - so he ordered him killed. And he said to the other: Do you bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. He said: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, so he let him go. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your companion took the excellent course, and you took the concession. What are you upon today? He said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah, and that he is a liar."
"326","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Raja' Abu al-Miqdam informed us, from al-Walid ibn Hisham, that on the day of Hunayn a man charged the idolaters alone without being ordered to. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Bilal, who called out: None disobedient shall enter Paradise."
"327","Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Sumay' al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Malik ibn Umayr al-Hanafi, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I met the enemy and met my father among them, and I heard an ugly remark from him about you, so I stabbed him with the spear and killed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent towards him. Then another came and said: O Prophet of Allah, I met my father but left him, for I wished someone else would deal with him. He said: So he remained silent towards him."
"328","Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar; a companion of mine narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, he said: No head was ever carried to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), not even on the day of Badr. A head was carried to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and he disapproved of it. The first to whom heads were carried was Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr."
"329","Abu Salih Mahbub ibn Musa narrated to us - Abu Ishaq informed us - from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, he said: Ri'yah al-Suhaymi came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Have my child and my property been raided? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for the property, it has been divided; as for the child, go, O so-and-so, with him - if he recognizes his child, hand them over to him. So he went with him and showed him to him. He said: So he recognized him. He said: Yes, hand him over to him. Abu Dawud said: It is narrated that he had accepted Islam before being raided. Abu Dawud said: It is narrated with a connected chain, but it is not sound; Isra'il narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara', and this is sounder."
"330","Muhammad ibn Uthman Abu al-Jumahir al-Tanukhi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Busr al-Hubrani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Adi al-Bahrani, from his brother Abd al-A'la, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he sent Ali on the day of Bi'r Khumm and saw a man with a Persian bow. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O owner of the bow, cast it away, for cursed is its bearer. Upon you are these Arab bows - and he pointed with his bow - with these and their likes, and spears and lances, Allah strengthens your religion, and through them Allah grants you mastery in the lands. Abu Dawud said: This hadith has been narrated with a connected chain, but it is not strong; and this Abdullah ibn Busr is not strong - Yahya ibn Sa'id used to weaken him."
"331","Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ma'dan ibn Hudayr al-Hadrami, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of those of my community who raid and take wages - meaning they strengthen themselves against their enemy - is like the mother of Musa, nursing her child and taking her wage."
"332","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrimah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a slain woman at al-Ta'if and said: Did I not forbid killing women? Who is the owner of this slain woman? A man of the people said: I am, O Messenger of Allah - I had her riding behind me and she wanted to throw me down and kill me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that she be buried."
"333","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, and Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) besieged the people of al-Ta'if, a woman appeared and uncovered her private part, saying: Here you are, shoot. A Muslim man shot her and did not miss that mark of hers. This is the wording of Sa'id; and in the hadith of Wuhayb: He did not miss killing her. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that she be buried."
"334","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Thawr, from Makhul, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set up catapults against the people of al-Ta'if."
"335","Abu Salih narrated to us, Abu Ishaq informed us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) besieged them - meaning the people of al-Ta'if - for a month. I said: Has it reached you that he shot at them with catapults? He denied that, saying: This is not known."
"336","Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Bishr informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed three men of Quraysh on the day of Badr as bound captives: al-Mut'im ibn Adi, al-Nadr ibn al-Harith and Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt. When he ordered the killing of al-Nadr, al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad said: My captive, O Messenger of Allah! He said: He used to say about the Book of Allah and about the Messenger of Allah what he used to say. He said that two or three times, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, enrich al-Miqdad from Your bounty. And al-Miqdad had captured al-Nadr. Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah said: Tu'mah ibn Adi, in place of al-Mut'im. Abu Dawud said: Al-Mut'im is an error; it is rather Tu'aymah ibn Adi. He, peace be upon him, said: Had al-Mut'im ibn Adi been alive and then spoken to me concerning these foul ones, I would have released them for him; and Wahshi was set free for killing Hamzah, in exchange for Tu'aymah."
"337","A chapter on ransoming with minors, and on one who finds his property among the spoils: Hannad narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent the remainder of the fifth - of the women and offspring - with Sa'id ibn Zayd to Najd, to sell them for him in exchange for horses and weapons. Abu Dawud said: This was mentioned concerning the raid of Qurayzah."
"338","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, he said: A man found his she-camel in the possession of (another) man, and the two brought the matter to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He established proof that it was his she-camel, and the other established proof that he had bought it from the enemy. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, take it for what he bought it for, and if you wish, leave it."
"339","On what a man accepts Islam with: Hannad narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, that al-Mughirah said: O Messenger of Allah, take the fifth from this wealth I seized from the caravan of Banu Malik, whom I killed. But the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused to grant him (that), because it was treacherous wealth, and said: As for Islam, we shall accept it from you."
"340","Ja'far ibn Musafir narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn Yahya al-Burlusi, from the coasts of Egypt, narrated to us; Haywah ibn Shurayh informed us, Uqayl informed me, from Ibn Shihab, that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah alighted with some companions of his at Aylah and drank wine until they became drunk and slept, while they were disbelievers, and before al-Mughirah had accepted Islam. Al-Mughirah rose against them and slaughtered them all, then took whatever they had, and traveled with it until he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Mughirah accepted Islam and handed the wealth to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of the news. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is taken by force is not subject to the fifth. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left the wealth in al-Mughirah's hand."
"341","A chapter on haste in travel: Ibn al-Musaffa narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah informed us, Hariz ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Habib ibn Ubayd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when returning from his raids and detachments, used to hasten on account of the scantiness of provisions."
"342","A chapter on what is said at the conquest: Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Salman; I heard al-Sha'bi saying: When (When the help of Allah and victory come) was revealed, whenever a conquest was granted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he would say: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, I turn to Allah and seek His forgiveness."
"343","A chapter on settling offspring on the coasts and frontiers: Umar ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Al-Walid ibn Muslim recited it to us, from al-Wadin ibn Ata', from Makhul and al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not leave offspring facing the enemy."
"344","A chapter on showing favor to offspring: Musaddad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abu al-Safar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Badr: Whoever captures Umm Hakim ibn Hizam, let him release her. A man of the Ansar had captured her by her braid; when he heard the caller of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he released her."
"345","A chapter on cutting trees: Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi narrated to us, Wahb, meaning Ibn Jarir, narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq; my father Ishaq ibn Yasar narrated to me, from al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: And Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Banu al-Nadir - and he mentioned the story - he said: So he marched to them and they fortified themselves; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut the palms and burned. When they saw the palms being cut and burned, they called out: O Muhammad, you used to forbid corruption, so what is with the cutting of palms and their burning? And some of the Muslims felt uneasy about that, so Allah revealed: (Whatever palm trees you cut or left standing), the verse."
"346","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: They were evacuated to Adhri'at and Ariha - meaning Banu al-Nadir. Allah the Exalted says: (And to disgrace the defiantly disobedient)."
"347","On wills: Ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A covenanted non-Muslim is held to the last of his two dispositions, when he is of sound mind."
"348","Abu Ma'mar Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata' al-Khurasani, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no bequest for an heir, unless the heirs wish it. Abu Dawud said: Ata' al-Khurasani did not meet Ibn Abbas, nor did he see him."
"349","Ibrahim ibn Marwan al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dweller within forty houses is a neighbor. He said: So I said to Ibn Shihab: How are forty houses? He said: Forty to his right, to his left, behind him and before him."
"350","The mudabbar (a slave promised freedom upon his master's death): Umar ibn Hisham al-Qibti narrated to us, Ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Hasan, meaning Ibn Salih, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed the mudabbar within the third (of the estate)."
"351","Hannad narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, that a man of Banu Udhrah freed his slave during his illness, having no wealth besides him; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to work off the two-thirds."
"352","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abu Qilabah, from a man of Banu Udhrah, that a man of them freed a slave of his at the time of his death; and he mentioned its meaning."
"353","On the laws of inheritance: Abu Kamil narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the grandmother a sixth as sustenance."
"354","Abd al-Salam ibn Mutahhar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave three grandmothers the sixth. I said: Who are they? He said: Your two grandmothers on your father's side, and your grandmother on your mother's side."
"355","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: I was told that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ... then he mentioned the like of it. (He said: So he asked) who are they? He said: The two grandmothers of the father: his father's mother and his mother's mother, and the grandmother of the mother: her mother's mother."
"356","Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a grandmother the sixth, though her son was alive."
"357","Ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: The first grandmother to whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave sustenance was a father's mother, though her son was alive."
"358","Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Anbari narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from al-Fadl ibn Dalham, from al-Hasan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave three grandmothers inheritance."
"359","Isa ibn Yunus al-Tarsusi narrated to us, Hajjaj, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An intentional or mistaken killer inherits nothing of the blood-money. Al-Zuhri said: He inherits from other than it. Abu Dawud said: Ma'mar, Salih ibn Kaysan and Yunus narrated the like from al-Zuhri, as the statement of Ibn al-Musayyib (mawquf)."
"360","Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Zayd, meaning Ibn Aslam, from Ata', that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode to Quba' seeking guidance (istikhara) concerning the inheritance of the paternal aunt and the maternal aunt, and it was revealed to him: There is no inheritance for them. Abu Dawud said: Its meaning is: They have no fixed share, but they inherit on account of kinship."
"361","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubayd, from a man from the people of Sham, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The child of the woman subjected to li'an (mutual imprecation), his 'asabah (paternal heirs) are the 'asabah of his mother."""
"362","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, Humayd — meaning Ibn 'Abd al-Rahman — narrated to me, from al-Hasan ibn Salih, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa narrated to me, he said: A man died leaving his daughter and his manumitters, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided the property between them in two halves, between his daughter and his manumitters."
"363","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad, that he said: Do you know what the daughter of Hamzah is to me? She was my sister through my mother, and she manumitted a slave of hers who then died leaving his daughter and his manumittress, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his inheritance between them in halves. Abu Dawud said: Several narrated it from 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad, that the daughter of Hamzah was the one who manumitted."
"364","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: A freed slave of Hamzah ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the daughter of Hamzah half and took (the other) half. Al-Husayn ibn 'Ali ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sharik said: Ibrahim ventured rashly into this statement, unless he heard something and narrated it, and he narrated little."
"365","Husayn ibn 'Ali ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Yahya — meaning Ibn Adam — narrated to us, 'Abd al-Salam — meaning Ibn Harb — narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr and others, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married 'Umarah bint Hamzah to Salamah ibn Abi Salamah though they had not reached maturity, then they died and inherited from one another."
"366","Musaddad narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Mu'allim, from al-Hasan, that a man from the polytheists went out performing Hajj, and when he returned departing, a Muslim man met him and killed him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to pay his blood-money to his family."
"367","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ishaq ibn 'Isa Abu Hisham narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, from 'Abd Rabbihi ibn al-Hakam, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) besieged the people of Ta'if, some slaves belonging to them came out to him and embraced Islam, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed them. When their masters later embraced Islam, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned the wala' (clientage) to them."
"368","Muhammad ibn al-Wazir al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Yahya — meaning Ibn Hassan — narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The inheritance of a people is not to be fragmented when it cannot bear division."""
"369","Muhammad ibn 'Awf narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ka'b narrated to us, 'Isa narrated to us, from Thawr, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Nusayr, the freed slave of Mu'awiyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the division that causes harm."
"370","Husayn ibn 'Ali ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Yahya — meaning Ibn Adam — narrated to us, 'Ammar ibn Zurayq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, ""They ask you for a ruling; say: Allah gives you a ruling concerning kalalah""? He said: ""Whoever leaves neither child nor parent, his heirs are kalalah."" Abu Dawud said: 'Ammar also narrated from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara', concerning kalalah: ""The summer verse suffices you."""
"371","'Isa ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Damrah, from Sa'd ibn 'Abdullah ibn Sa'd, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whatever shepherd seeks profit at the expense of his flock, his flock is ruined."""
"372","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad — meaning Ibn Ja'far — narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah: I heard al-Sha'bi (say), that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to take the pledge from the women, a Qatari cloak was brought and he placed it upon his hand, then said: ""I do not shake hands with women."""
"373","'Umar ibn Hisham al-Qibti narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far al-Razi, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abu al-'Aliyah, he said: When booty was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would divide it into five fifths, then take a handful from the entire fifth and say: ""This is for the Ka'bah."" Then he would say: ""Do not assign a share to Allah, for to Allah belong the Hereafter and the first (life)."" Then he would take a share for himself, a share for the near relatives, a share for the orphans, a share for the poor, and a share for the wayfarer."
"374","Khushaysh ibn Asram narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Muhriz narrated to us: I asked al-Hasan about the anfal (spoils), he said: The spoils used to be gathered, and when gathered the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a share from them called the share of al-safi (the choicest part), which Allah assigned to him, then he narrated the hadith."
"375","Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked what is disliked among sacrificial animals and camels. He said: ""The one-eyed, the emaciated, and the one whose udders are all dried up."""
"376","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, from Yahya, that Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to him, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman and Sulayman ibn Yasar, that it reached them that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Sacrificial meat (may be kept) until the crescent of Muharram, for whoever wishes to delay that."""
"377","Musaddad narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from al-Salt, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The slaughter of a Muslim is lawful, whether he mentioned the name of Allah or not; if he mentioned, he mentioned none but the name of Allah."""
"378","Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, Ja'far narrated to us, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the 'aqiqah which Fatimah offered for al-Hasan and al-Husayn: ""Send a leg of it to the midwife, and eat and feed others, and do not break any of its bones."""
"379","'Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Malik, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, that he said: Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), weighed the hair of al-Hasan, al-Husayn, Zaynab, and Umm Kulthum, and gave silver equal to its weight in charity."
"380","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', he said: There is no harm in making roast meat, meaning from the 'aqiqah."
"381","Al-Nufayli narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us — this being the hadith of Zuhayr — 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from 'Amir, that a Bedouin gave a gazelle as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: ""Where did you get this?"" He said: I shot it yesterday and pursued it, but it eluded me until evening overtook me, so I returned. In the morning I followed its trail and found it in a cave, or among stones, with my arrowhead in it which I recognize. He said: ""It spent the night away from you, and I do not feel safe that some venomous creature did not help you against it. I have no need for it."""
"382","Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi 'A'ishah, from Abu Razin, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with game and said: I shot it at night and it eluded me, then I found my arrow in it the next morning, and I recognized my arrow. He said: ""The night is a great creation among Allah's creation; perhaps something aided you against it and kept it away from you."""
"383","It was narrated to me from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from 'Abbad ibn Ishaq, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade (killing) swallows, the shelter-seekers of houses."
"384","Ibrahim ibn Marwan al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from 'Irak ibn Malik, that he used to say: The mitran (slaughter instrument) may be slaughtered with. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about that and said: ""It is lawful."""
"385","Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever swears by a surah from the Book of Allah, upon him is, for every verse of it, a binding oath; if he wishes he may fulfill it, and if he wishes he may break it."""
"386","Ibrahim ibn Musa al-Razi narrated to us, 'Isa narrated to us, from 'Awf, from al-Hasan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the same in meaning."
"387","Harun ibn 'Abbad al-Azdi narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Layth ibn Sa'd, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah and Rashid ibn Sa'd: A woman gave dates as a gift to 'A'ishah, and she ate some while some dates remained. The woman said: I adjure you to eat all of it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The sin is upon the one who forces (another to break an oath)."""
"388","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Faris narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not appoint a judge until he died, nor did Abu Bakr nor 'Umar, except that he said to a man at the end of his caliphate: ""Spare me (the burden of) some of the people's affairs."""
"389","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, with the same meaning, he said: Until it was near the end of his life — meaning the time of 'Umar — when he said to Yazid, son of the sister of Namir: ""Spare me some of the people's affairs,"" meaning the minor ones."
"390","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is summoned to a judge among the judges and does not respond is a wrongdoer."""
"391","'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah al-Makhzumi al-Madani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-'Umari, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) employed 'Ali ibn Abi Talib over Yemen, 'Ali said: He summoned me and advised me, saying to him: ""Give precedence to the lowly before the noble, give precedence to the weak before the strong, and give precedence to men before women."""
"392","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would judge with a judgment, then the Qur'an would descend afterwards contrary to it, so he would carry out what he had judged the first time and henceforth judge according to what the Qur'an brought."
"393","Hilal ibn Bishr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Qays narrated to us: I heard Zayd ibn Aslam (say), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes possession of something for ten years, it is his."""
"394","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah and Humayd, from al-Hasan, that a man from Quraysh stole a she-camel, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off his hand, yet his testimony remained acceptable."
"395","'Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz — meaning Ibn Muhammad — narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd — meaning Ibn al-Muhajir — from Talhah ibn 'Abdullah — meaning Ibn 'Awf — from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""There is no testimony for an adversary nor for one under suspicion."" Abu Dawud said: Al-zanin is the accused, al-jinnah is one in whom there is madness, and al-hinnah is the spiteful."
"396","Al-Qasim ibn 'Isa narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Hakam ibn Muslim, from 'Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""The testimony of one under suspicion and rancor and madness is not permissible."" Ibn Abi Dhi'b said: One of suspicion and rancor."
"397","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Bukayr: He heard Ibn al-Musayyib say: Two men disputed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over something, and each of them brought upright witnesses of equal number, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots between them and said: ""O Allah, You judge between them."""
"398","Abu Tawbah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq — meaning al-Fazari — informed us, from Abu Ishaq — meaning al-Shaybani — from al-Qasim — meaning Ibn 'Abd al-Rahman: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not compel people in their oaths to what they do not know."""
"399","Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Abu Usamah and Yazid narrated to us, from al-Sa'q ibn Hazn, from al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a man is asked about his brother, he has a choice: if he wishes he may remain silent, and if he wishes he may speak and tell the truth."" One of them said: Concerning the man."
"400","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: A man passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: ""Who knows him?"" A man said: I know him by his face, but I do not know him by his name. He said: ""That is not (real) knowledge."""
"401","Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The protected zone of an ancient well is fifty cubits, and the protected zone of a newly begun well is twenty-five cubits."" Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib added on his own: And the protected zone of a well for irrigation is three hundred cubits."
"402","'Amr ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, al-Zubaydi narrated to us: al-Zuhri narrated to us: The Sunnah and the judicial practice follow the meaning of the entire hadith of Sufyan, stating for each of them in every direction: this is the protected zone, adding the word ""qulab"" in place of well, and adding: The protected zone of a spring is five hundred cubits in every direction. This is the protected zone for excavations permitted by the authority, unless a people hold land upon which they embraced Islam or which they purchased."
"403","'Abbad ibn Musa narrated to us, Talhah — meaning Ibn Yahya al-Ansari — narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to me, from 'Imran, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled concerning the protected zone of a palm tree as its length."
"404","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-Hamadhani narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Sallam ibn Miskin narrated to us, from al-Hasan, he said: Some people fought with stones and a slain man was found among them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered their detention, then he related the hadith."
"405","Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Abu Harun al-Madani, he said: In the house of al-'Abbas there was a spout pouring into the mosque, then 'Umar came and removed it. Al-'Abbas said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) himself placed it with his hand. 'Umar said: ""You shall have no ladder except my back until you restore it to its place."" Abu Dawud said: This is the brother of 'Isa the grocer, Abu Harun, while 'Isa is the tailor — the grocer and the clothes-beater — and he is 'Isa ibn Maysarah, and his brother is unobjectionable."
"406","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Qattan narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman — meaning Ibn Maghra' — narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from his uncle Wasi' ibn Habban, he said: Abu Lubabah had a date-cluster in the garden of a man, so he spoke to him saying: You tread upon my garden to reach your cluster; I shall give you one like it in your garden, so remove it from me. He refused him, so he spoke to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it. He said: ""O Abu Lubabah, take a cluster like yours, join it to your property, and withhold from your companion what he dislikes."" He said: I will not do it. He said: ""Then go and cut for him a cluster like his into his garden, then build a wall above that, for there is no harm nor reciprocal harm in Islam."" Abu Dawud said: Al-'adhq with a fathah is the palm tree, and al-'idhq with a kasrah is the cluster."
"407","'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, from 'Abdullah Ibn al-Mubarak — and I read it to Sa'id ibn Ya'qub from Ibn Mubarak — from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not cause harm to one another in digging."" Sa'id added: That is when a man digs beside another man to take away his water."
"408","Malik ibn 'Abd al-Wahid al-Misma'i narrated to us, Rawh and Wahb narrated to us, both saying: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us: I heard 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb (say): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the woman to mourn her husband until her waiting period ends, seven days over her father, and three days over any besides them."
"409","Mahmud ibn Khalid and 'Amr ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, both saying: al-Walid narrated to us, from Ibn Jabir, from Makhul, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Attend your dying ones, question them, for they see, and prompt them with La ilaha illa Allah."""
"410","'Abd al-Hamid ibn Bakkar al-Bayruti narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Isma'il informed me, from Abu Salamah Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from Yahya ibn Jabir, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what nullifies the reward for a calamity? He said: ""That a man clap his right hand upon his left."" And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clapped his right hand upon his left."
"411","Qutaybah narrated to us, Yahya — meaning Ibn Sulaym — narrated to us, from 'Imran al-Qasir, he said: The lamp of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, so he said: ""Inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi raji'un."" 'A'ishah said: This is but a lamp. He said: ""Everything that displeases the believer is a calamity."""
"412","Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Salamah al-Makhzumi, he said: When news of the deaths of Ja'far and Zayd arrived, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the house of Zayd. When he was at the door, a daughter of Zayd met him bursting into weeping before him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wept until he sobbed. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this? He said: ""The longing of a beloved for a beloved."""
"413","Harun ibn 'Abbad narrated to us, Abu Bakr — meaning Ibn 'Ayyash — narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Sahl, from Makhul, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a woman dies among men with no woman besides her, and a man among women with no man besides him, they are both given tayammum and buried, and they are in the position of one who finds no water."""
"414","Hannad narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: 'Ali sought from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what is sought from the dead, but did not find it. So he said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, you were pleasant in life and in death."
"415","Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: A red striped cloth that he had acquired on the day of Khaybar was placed in the lahd (niche grave) of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), because the land of Madinah is saline. Abu Dawud said: It is musnad (connected) except parts of the wording in which it became peculiar, so it became mursal."
"416","Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Anbari narrated to us, 'Abdah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Murrah al-Qurashi, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken (into the grave) from the direction of the qiblah, and he was not lowered straight down."
"417","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Faris narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Abu Ishaq — meaning al-Fazari — narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a single salutation over the funeral."
"418","'Abbad ibn Musa and Sulayman ibn Dawud al-'Ataki narrated to us with the same meaning, that Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to them, from his father, he said: It reached him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed Nu'aym ibn Mas'ud in the grave and removed the pillows with his mouth."
"419","Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Ziyad — meaning Ibn Tha'lab — from Abu al-Mundhir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw three handfuls (of earth) into a grave."
"420","Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, that Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to them: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, he said: I saw the grave of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a span or about a span (high)."
"421","'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Murrah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: The grave of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was made with excavated earth heaped (nabath) and was not leveled flat."
"422","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I saw the graves of the martyrs raised in humps, meaning mounds."
"423","'Abdullah ibn Maslamah ibn Qa'nab and 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Aban ibn Salih narrated to us, that 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to them, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad — meaning Ibn 'Umar — from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sprinkled (water) over the grave of his son Ibrahim. Ibn 'Umar added in his hadith: It was the first grave to be sprinkled upon, and he said when he was buried and finished at his head: ""Peace be upon you."" I know only that he said: He threw (earth) upon it with his hand. Al-Qa'nabi did not say: meaning Ibn 'Umar."
"424","'Amr ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, (ha') and Muhammad ibn 'Awf narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Safwan, from Abu al-Yaman al-Hawzani, he said: When Abu Talib, the uncle of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and met his funeral procession. Ibn 'Awf said: He walked keeping to its side saying: ""Kinship has done good to you, and may you be rewarded with good."" And he did not stand over his grave. Ibn 'Awf added: He did not seek forgiveness for him. And 'Amr did not mention the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"425","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj: Muhammad ibn 'Ali informed me, that the funeral of Ibrahim, son of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), was carried upon a horse's saddle-frame."
"426","Ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Husayn, from Abu Malik, he said: On the day of Uhud the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought Hamzah ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib; he was placed, then nine were brought and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over them. They were lifted while Hamzah was left, then nine more were brought and placed, and he prayed over them seven prayers, until he prayed over seventy men, Hamzah among them in every prayer he prayed."
"427","Hannad narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Ata', from al-Sha'bi, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over Hamzah on the day of Uhud seventy prayers, beginning with Hamzah: he prayed over him, then kept calling the martyrs and praying over them while Hamzah remained in place."
"428","Ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned two men between Makkah and Madinah; he prayed over one of them and did not pray over the other. Abu Dawud said: It has been narrated connected (muttasil) with other wording."
"429","Al-Nufayli narrated to us, Miskin narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn 'Abdullah, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at a funeral, grief overcame him; he would engage much in inward reflection and speak little."
"430","Hannad ibn al-Sari and 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, from Wa'il ibn Dawud: I heard al-Bahiyy say: When Ibrahim, son of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died — he died at six months — the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over him at the sitting places. Abu Dawud said: Hannad narrated: He is indeed truthful, and he indeed has a nursing mother in Paradise."
"431","I read to Sa'id ibn Ya'qub al-Talaqani: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to you, from Ya'qub ibn al-Qa'qa', from 'Ata', that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over his son Ibrahim when he was seventy nights old."
"432","Ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn 'Adi, from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over those slain at Uhud."
"433","Ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned two men between Makkah and Madinah; he prayed over one of them and did not pray over the other. Abu Dawud said: It has been narrated connected (muttasil) with other wording."
"434","Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sulayman — meaning Ibn Kathir — narrated to us, from Husayn, from Abu Malik: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought Hamzah and nine were brought, and he prayed over them — the hadith in full as it preceded."
"435","Hannad narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Ata', from al-Sha'bi, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over Hamzah — the hadith as it preceded shortly before."
"436","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Ibn Dawud narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a slave girl menstruates, it is not proper for anything of her to be seen except her face and her hands up to the joint."""
"437","'Abdullah ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Abu 'Asim, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ziyad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that anything of the two sandals protrude over the feet."
"438","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith, he said: I came to Madinah and was brought two sandals which they claimed were the sandals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with two straps, the ends of their thongs folded into their knots. I mentioned it to Muhammad, so he sent for his sandals on the spot and altered them."
"439","'Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khalid, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith, he said: I saw the sandals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with two front straps."
"440","It was read to al-Harith ibn Miskin while I was present: Ibn al-Qasim informed you, from Malik — and he was asked about the sandal of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whether he had seen it: how was its shape? He said: It was toward roundness, its middle narrowed at its rear, narrowed and heeled at its back. I said: Did it have two straps? He said: That is what I believe, with the family of Rabi'ah al-Makhzumi from their mother Umm Kulthum."
"441","Ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us: Ibn 'Awn narrated to us, he said: I came to a shoemaker in Madinah and ordered him to make my sandals with two front straps. He said to me: Shall I not make them as I saw the sandals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: With whom did you see them? He said: With Fatimah bint 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abbas. I said: Then make them so. He made both of them on the right pattern."
"442","Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Yazid al-Haddadi Abu Hashim narrated to me: Abu 'Abd al-Da'im narrated to me, from Abu Malih, that the sandal of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke, or the strap of his sandal, so he walked in one sandal until he repaired the other."
"443","Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id — meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub — narrated to us: Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to me, he said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a mirror and a kohl container."
"444","Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was recognized by the fragrance of perfume."
"445","'Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, that al-Hakam ibn al-Salt narrated to them, from 'Abdullah ibn Muti', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whenever an honor is presented to a person, let him not fail to take from it, little or much."""
"446","Nusayr ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from 'Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is offered perfume or sweetness, let him not refuse it, for it is pleasant in scent and light to carry."""
"447","'Amr ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, Marwan — meaning Ibn Mu'awiyah — narrated to us, from 'Uthman ibn al-Aswad: He heard Mujahid say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man with a long beard and said: ""Why does one of you disfigure himself?"" And he saw a man with disheveled head — meaning unkempt hair — and said: ""Quiet! Treat your hair well or shave it."""
"448","Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from al-Awza'i, from Harun ibn Ri'ab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped, then he said to a man: ""Bury it, lest a dog uncover it."""
"449","Ibn Nufayl narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, a woman of my family narrated to me, from Mulaykah bint 'Amr, that cow's ghee was prescribed to her for a pain in her throat. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Its milk is a cure, its ghee is a medicine, and its meat is a disease."""
"450","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Faris narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is cupped on Wednesday and Saturday and is afflicted with vitiligo, let him blame none but himself."" Abu Dawud said: This has been narrated with a chain, but it is not sound."
"451","Abu Ma'mar and Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, both saying: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seeks cupping, let him be cupped on Saturday. Ahmad al-Duri said: And Hafs said: I narrated it to Sufyan al-Thawri, so he summoned the cupper on the spot and was cupped."
"452","Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Raja, who said: I asked al-Hasan about the nushrah, and he said: It was mentioned to me from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: It is from the work of Satan."
"453","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya Abu Muhammad and Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh, in the same meaning, both saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a writing on a shoulder blade, and he said: Sufficient misguidance for a people is that they seek a book other than their Book, to a prophet other than their Prophet. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: Is it not sufficient for them that We sent down to you the Book which is recited to them."
"454","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, that Umar passed by some Jews and heard them mentioning a supplication from the Torah, so he copied it, then brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and began to read it, while the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to change. A man said: O Ibn al-Khattab, do you not see what is on the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So Umar laid down the book, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent me as the Seal, and I have been given comprehensive speech and its seals, and speech has been made concise for me, so let not the confused ones distract you. I said to Abu Qilabah: What are the confused ones? He said: The bewildered."
"455","Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Ala, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his hadith would abrogate one another just as the Quran abrogates one another."
"456","Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Abu Khalid, from Ibn Ajlan, from Tawus, from Mu'adh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not hasten tribulation before it descends, for if you do not do so, the Muslims will not lack among them one who, when he speaks, is guided aright or granted success; but if you hasten, paths will branch out with you here and here and here."
"457","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd, meaning al-Laythi, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned something similar in meaning."
"458","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thawr narrated to us, from Ma'mar, who said: I said to al-Zuhri: Why are the blind, the lame, and the sick mentioned here? My uncle Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah narrated to them that the Muslims, when they went out to fight, would leave behind their infirm, and would hand over to them the keys to their doors, saying: We have permitted you to eat from what is in our houses. But they would scruple about that, saying: We will not enter them while they are absent. So this verse was revealed as a concession for them."
"459","Hajjaj ibn Abi Ya'qub narrated to us, Ya'qub, meaning Ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah and Ibn al-Musayyib, that men of knowledge used to narrate that this verse, There is no blame upon the blind, was only revealed because the Muslims were eager to march forth with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the path of Allah, so they would give their keys to their infirm dependents, saying to them: We have permitted you. Then he mentioned something similar and more complete."
"460","Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from al-Zuhri, from Aishah, who said: The Muslims were eager, and he mentioned something similar. Abu Dawud said: And the correct one is the hadith of Ya'qub and Ma'mar."
"461","Ibn al-Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Ibn Thawban narrated to us, from his father: I asked Makhul: Who among people is most entitled to lead them at food? Makhul said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam, or the owner of the food, or the best of them. Then he said: Stretch forth your hand, O Abu Ubaydah."
"462","Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, from Abu Amr. Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, with its meaning, and he said: And they held that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was fasting that day."
"463","Ishaq ibn Suwayd al-Ramli narrated to us, Sawwar ibn Umarah narrated to us, Masarrah, meaning Ibn Ma'bad, narrated to me. He said: al-Zuhri and Sulayman ibn Musa narrated to me, both saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not eat raw meat until three days pass for it, or fire touches it."
"464","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Wasil ibn Abi Jamil, from Mujahid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked seven things from the sheep: the bladder, the gallbladder, the gland, the penis, the vulva, and the testicles."
"465","Ibrahim ibn Marwan ibn Muhammad al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad, meaning al-Umari, narrated to me, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not eat the hip, saying: Its outer side is sciatica and its inner side is paralysis."
"466","Musaddad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from his father, from a man of the Ansar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the two lobes of the heart."
"467","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah ibn Sufyan narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, that he heard al-Zuhri denying that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted date-wine from jars after his prohibition, and reviling whoever claims that."
"468","Abu Kamil al-Fudayl ibn al-Husayn al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Salih ibn Salih narrated to us. Abu Ma'shar narrated to us that a man applied depilatory paste to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he reached the pubic region the man held back, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) applied it to himself."
"469","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Adhrami narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab, meaning Ibn Ata, narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never used depilatory paste, nor did Abu Bakr, nor Umar, nor Uthman."
"470","Qutaybah narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you bathe except with a person near him who does not look, while close to him and speaking to him."
"471","With the same chain, from al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not bathe in the open desert unless you see a screen; and if you do not find one, let one of you draw a line like a room, then mention Allah and bathe within it."
"472","Ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Salman, informed me, from Amr, the freedman of al-Muttalib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the one who looks and the one who is looked at."
"473","Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting with Abu Bakr, and that was when the first spathe of the date-palm was first seen. Abu Bakr saw a spathe, the first spathe seen in Medina, and rejoiced, saying: A spathe! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at it and said: O Allah, do not take away from us any good that You have given us, or any good of what You have given us."
"474","Ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, who said: Whenever the first fruits were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would place them on his eyes, then eat some of them, then say: O Allah, just as You have fed us its first, feed us its last, and bless it for us."
"475","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Faris narrated to us, Abu Asim and Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Yunus al-Ayli, from Ibn Shihab, that whenever the first fruits were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would kiss them and place them on his eyes."
"476","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Mahri narrated to us, from Ibn Wahb, Haywah and Ibn Lahi'ah informed me, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a wall that had leaned or cracked, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered up his garments, then hastened his pace until he passed it, and said to his Companions: Hasten. Abu Dawud said: And it has been narrated with a connected chain, but it is nothing."
"477","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, and Abu al-Mughirah, both saying: Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you calls his brother and he says to him: At your service, let him not say: Before you, but let him say: May Allah answer you with what you love."
"478","Abbas al-Anbari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, a man of the people of Iraq informed us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Blue eyes are a good omen. Abu Dawud said: Pharaoh was blue-eyed, and the hamstringer of the she-camel was blue-eyed."
"479","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim, meaning al-Ta'ifi, narrated to us, from a man, from al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No partisanship enters a man except that an equal amount of faith leaves him as entered him of partisanship."
"480","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade saying of Abdullah and al-Miqdad that they are not of Quraysh. Abu Dawud said: Meaning Ibn Mas'ud."
"481","Musa ibn Marwan al-Raqqi narrated to us, al-Mu'afa ibn Imran narrated to us, from Thawr, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what is prudence? He said: To consult one of sound judgment, then obey him."
"482","Muhammad ibn al-Wazir narrated to us, that Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to them, saying: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, and he mentioned the like of that, and he said: One of understanding."
"483","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and al-Nufayli narrated to us, both saying: Hafs narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kindness to parents suffices in place of jihad."
"484","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abu Hazim, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever strikes his father, kill him. Ibrahim said: I mentioned it to Sufyan, and he said: I have heard it from Abu Hazim."
"485","Ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub, from Ata ibn Dinar al-Hudhali, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the two parents has the greater right? He said: She who carried him between the two sides, suckled him with the two breasts, nursed him upon the two thighs, and ransomed him with both parents."
"486","Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Amr ibn Sa'id ibn al-As, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The right of the eldest brother over the younger is the right of the father over his child."
"487","Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Malik, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, shall I seek permission to enter upon my mother? He said: Yes. The man said: I live with her in the house. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Would you like to see her naked? He said: No. He said: Then seek permission to enter upon her."
"488","Nusayr ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Bakr ibn Amr informed us, that Safwan ibn Sulaym informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umm Ayman, who is the mother of Usamah: How are you this morning, or how are you this evening? She said: Well, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Amen; may Allah keep you well."
"489","Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of a group gives greeting, it suffices for them. Abu Dawud said: And it has been narrated with a connected chain, but it is weak."
"490","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Mushir, from al-Ajlah, from al-Sha'bi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Ja'far ibn Abi Talib, embraced him, and kissed him between his eyes. Abu Dawud said: This has been narrated with a connected chain but it is not sound."
"491","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, that a Jew milked for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O Allah, beautify him; so his hair turned black."
"492","Amr ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Sa'id, from al-Yasa' ibn al-Mughirah, who said: Khalid ibn al-Walid complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the narrowness of his house, and he said: Expand upward into the sky."
"493","Abdullah ibn Muhammad and Ali ibn Sahl al-Ramliyyan narrated to us, both saying: al-Walid narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Ala, from Atiyyah ibn Qays, who said: The apartments of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were of palm stalks. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on one of his expeditions, and Umm Salamah was well-off, so she replaced the stalks with bricks. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is this? She said: I wanted to shield myself from the gaze of people. He said: O Umm Salamah, the worst thing in which the wealth of a Muslim man is spent is building."
"494","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, from Abu al-Aliyah, that al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib built an upper room, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Tear it down. He said: Shall I give in charity the like of its cost in the path of Allah? He said: Tear it down; so he tore it down."
"495","Ghassan ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Qays, who said: I saw the apartments of palm stalks covered on the outside with haircloth, and I reckon the width of the apartment from the door of the room to the door of the house was about six or seven cubits, and I estimated the inner room at ten cubits, and I think its height was between eight and nine, and the like; and I stood at the door of Aishah and it faced west."
"496","Ghassan narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Hurayth ibn al-Sa'ib: I heard al-Hasan say: I used to enter the houses of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during the caliphate of Uthman ibn Affan and touch their ceilings with my hand."
"497","I recited to Qutaybah ibn Sa'id: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to you, from Muhammad ibn Hilal, who said: The door of Aishah was of teak."
"498","Harun ibn Abbad al-Azdi narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Hanzali, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a writing on the ground and said to a youth with him: What is this? He said: In the name of Allah. He said: May Allah curse whoever did this, and do not place the name of Allah except in its proper place. He said: Then I saw Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz see a son of his write the remembrance of Allah on the wall and he struck him."
"499","Muhammad ibn al-Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from al-Wadin ibn Ata, from Yazid ibn Marthad, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The spider is a devil, so kill it."
"500","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, from Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, from Hanan, from Abu Uthman, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is given sweet basil, let him not refuse it, for it has come out of Paradise."
"501","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world is cursed, and cursed is what is in it, except what is for Allah of it."
"502","al-Hasan ibn Shawkar narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, meaning al-Majishun, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Ibrahim ibn Murrah, who said: A scorpion stung the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What is with it, may Allah curse it; it cares neither for a prophet nor for anyone else."
"503","Muhammad ibn al-Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from al-Wadin ibn Ata, from Yazid ibn Marthad al-Mudda'i, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The spider is a devil, so kill it."
"504","Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Sallam narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Wuhayb. I heard Kharijah ibn Zayd say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most dignified of people in his sitting; he would hardly extend anything of his limbs."
"505","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from al-Awza'i, from Urwah ibn Ruwaym, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing my Lord forbade me after the worship of idols was drinking wine and quarreling with men."
"506","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Abthar narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu al-Safar, from Ali ibn Rabi'ah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Mecca, he set out at once for Ta'if, with Abu Bakr with him, and with him the two sons of Sa'id ibn al-As. Abu Bakr said: Whose grave is this? They said: The grave of Sa'id ibn al-As. Abu Bakr said: May Allah curse the occupant of this grave, for he used to oppose Allah and His Messenger. The two sons of Sa'id said: May Allah curse Abu Quhafah, for he would neither honor the guest nor ward off disgrace. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Reviling the dead angers the living; so when you revile the polytheists, revile them all together."
"507","al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: A man came to al-Abbas and said: What of al-Ghaytalah, the soothsayer of Banu Sahm, in the Fire with Abd al-Muttalib? So al-Abbas struck his nose. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is with one of you that he hurts his brother in a matter even if it is true?"
"508","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us, from Ali ibn Husayn, that Abdullah ibn Ubayy said: If we return to Medina, the mightier will surely expel the lowlier from it; that was on the expedition of Tabuk. He said: And the last of the people had not yet alighted. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: March on, march on. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not command a man of his people to strike his neck? He said: I dislike that one should be angered thereby whom I do not wish to anger."
"509","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Mahri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah informed me, from al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Hadrami, raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Straighten your circles, for when the angels come to sit and find crookedness in them, they turn back."
"510","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Tariq, from al-Sha'bi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a noble man of a people comes to you, honor him. Abu Dawud said: It has been narrated with a connected chain, but it is nothing."
"511","Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd, meaning Ibn Ibrahim, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When there are two, the third shall not approach them until he seeks their permission."
"512","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Abd al-A'la ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah informed me, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, who said: I heard that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man is not separated from his father. I was sitting with an uncle of mine when he came, and we made room for him between us. Abd al-A'la said: This is but my uncle. He said: Yes; the paternal uncle is a father in the Book of Allah."
"513","Abu Salih al-Antaki narrated to us, Abu Ishaq informed us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not seize anyone on mere accusation, nor believe anyone against anyone."
"514","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Hafs informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab saw the kurraj in Medina and said: As for me, had I not seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leave you alone, I would not have left you."
"515","Hannad and Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Ziyad ibn Abi Muslim, who said: I heard Salih Abu al-Khalil narrating that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the swings to be cut down. Hannad said: That he heard it."
"516","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he passed by people gathered around a man who was making them laugh. He said: What is this? They said: A man imitating the donkey, making his companions laugh. He said: Glory be to Allah; what security has this one, when Allah has made his form beautiful, against being transformed into the form of a donkey?"
"517","Kathir ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from Yahya ibn Jabir, from Yazid ibn Shurayh, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things are of gambling: wagering, playing with dice, and whistling at pigeons."
"518","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, that Muhammad ibn Urwah informed him, from Urwah, who said: A woman died whom the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to laugh at. Bilal said of her: Poor her, she has found rest. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Only one who is forgiven finds rest."
"519","Harun ibn Zayd narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Aishah, who said: I never heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) attribute anyone except to religion."
"520","Sahl ibn Salih narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Mina, from Ibn Jawdan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever apologizes to his Muslim brother and he does not accept it from him bears the same as the taker of unlawful tax."
"521","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him, but found nothing with him. She said: O Messenger of Allah, promise me. He said: A promise is a gift."
"522","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Ibn Wahb, from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Zayd ibn Aslam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The solemn pledge of the believer is a binding right. Abu Dawud said: Meaning his promise."
"523","Hisham ibn Khalid narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, al-Wadin ibn Ata narrated to us. Yazid ibn Marthad al-Mudda'i narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sneezes or belches, let him not raise his voice with them, for Satan loves that the voice be raised with them."
"524","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd informed me, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, who said: A man kept removing something from the face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it seemed to annoy the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you removes something from his brother, let him show it to him."
"525","Nasr ibn Asim narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Harmalah: I went out with Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib while he was holding my hand. I raised my head and saw the crescent. I said: The crescent, O Abu Muhammad. He raised his head and said: I believe in the One who created you, fashioned you, and proportioned you. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say thus."
"526","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Aban narrated to us. Qatadah narrated to us that it reached him that whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw the crescent, he would say: A crescent of good and right guidance, a crescent of good and right guidance; I believe in the One who created you, three times. Then he would say: Praise be to Allah who has taken away such-and-such month and brought such-and-such month. Abu Dawud said: It has been narrated with a connected chain, but it is not sound."
"527","Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us, that Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed them, from Abu Hilal, from Qatadah, that whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw the crescent, he would turn his face away from it."
"528","Muhammad ibn Qudamah ibn A'yan narrated to us, Jarir narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Abdullah ibn Uwaymir, who said: I was with Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, and I pointed with my hand toward the cloud. He said: Do not do it, for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade pointing to it."
"529","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade pointing to the rain."
"530","Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, Marwan narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us. Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to me that some people heard thunder and uttered the takbir. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear thunder, glorify Allah and do not utter the takbir."
"531","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Habib, from one of our shaykhs, who said: Whenever a pleasing matter came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would say: Praise be to Allah, the Bestower, the Generous, by whose blessings good deeds are completed; and when a displeasing matter came to him, he would say: Praise be to Allah in every circumstance. Abu Dawud said: It has been narrated with a connected chain, and in it are weak hadiths, and it is not sound."
"532","al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb narrated to us, Miskin narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Ibrahim ibn Tarif, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi. One whom I do not suspect narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The most fearful of what I fear for you after me are three: what is opened for you of the bloom and adornment of the world, men who interpret the Quran contrary to its interpretation, and the slip of a scholar. Then he said: Shall I not inform you of the way out of that? When the world is opened for you, thank Allah; take what you recognize of interpretation, and what you doubt, refer it to Allah, Mighty and Majestic; wait for the scholar to return to the truth, and do not pounce upon his slip."
"533","Abd al-Salam ibn Atiq al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Mushir narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to me, Hisham ibn al-Ghaz narrated to me, from Makhul, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has given me the Quran and with it wisdom twice over."
"534","Isa ibn Hammad narrated to us, al-Layth informed us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Abu Sa'id, the freedman of Ibn Kurayz, from al-Hasan al-Basri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever commits an offense or shelters an offender, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither repentance nor ransom is accepted from him. They said: What is the offense, O Messenger of Allah? He said: An innovation without precedent, a mutilation without legal cause, a plunder without right."
"535","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, who said: Gabriel, peace be upon him, used to descend upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the Sunnah just as he descended upon him with the Quran, teaching it to him just as he taught him the Quran."
"536","Musa narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ash'ath al-Huddani, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The excellence of the speech of Allah over all other speech is like the excellence of Allah, Mighty and Exalted, over all His creation."
"537","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Faris narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from Zayd ibn Artah, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will never return to Allah with anything better than what came forth from Him, meaning His speech."
"538","Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Salih narrated to me. Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit al-Jumahi narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant but that superstition will enter his heart; so when he feels that, let him say: I am the servant of Allah; what Allah wills; there is no power except through Allah; none brings good deeds except Allah, and none removes evil except Allah; I bear witness that Allah is capable of all things; then let him proceed on his way."
"539","Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Ali ibn Umar ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina and said: O company of Quraysh, you love livestock, so keep few of them, for you are the land of least rain; plow, for plowing is blessed, and place many skulls in it."
"540","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, al-Darawardi narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Hafs, my father informed me, that he heard Umar ibn Ali ibn Husayn and Abdullah ibn Anbasah mentioning the skulls placed in crops. Umar ibn Ali ibn Husayn said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only commanded that because of the evil eye."
"541","Abu Salih narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Simt, from al-Nu'man, from Makhul, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined Abu Hurayrah, then said: When you go forth to fight, and he mentioned things, saying: Do not burn a palm tree nor drown it, and do not harm a believer."
"542","It was narrated to me from Ibn Wahb, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim, the freedman of Abd al-Rahman, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then he mentioned something similar, and said: Do not burn a palm tree nor drown it, do not cut a fruitful tree, do not kill an animal for which you have no need, and beware of harming the believer."
"543","Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jabir said: Makhul narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And whoever among the Jews follows us has our protection, neither wronged nor aided against."
